":"After multiple attempts, Churchill gained admission to the Royal Military College, Sandhurst, beginning his military training.","details":null,"id":"797","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Entered Sandhurst","year":"1893"},{"description":"Churchill graduated eighth in his class and was commissioned as a Second Lieutenant in the 4th Queen's Own Hussars.","details":null,"id":"798","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Graduated from Sandhurst","year":"1894"},{"description":"Churchill traveled to Cuba as a military observer and war correspondent, gaining valuable combat and journalism experience.","details":null,"id":"799","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Military Observer in Cuba","year":"1895"},{"description":"Churchill's father, Lord Randolph Churchill, died, profoundly influencing Winston's determination to achieve political success.","details":null,"id":"800","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Death of Father","year":"1895"},{"description":"Churchill served with the British Army in India, spending much of his free time reading history, politics, and philosophy.","details":null,"id":"801","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Served in India","year":"1896"},{"description":"Churchill fought in the Malakand Campaign in British India and published his first successful military account.","details":null,"id":"802","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Malakand Campaign","year":"1897"},{"description":"Churchill participated in the Battle of Omdurman in Sudan and later published 'The River War' describing the campaign.","details":null,"id":"803","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Battle of Omdurman","year":"1898"},{"description":"Churchill resigned from active military service to pursue journalism and a career in British politics.","details":null,"id":"804","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Resigned from Army","year":"1899"},{"description":"While reporting on the Second Boer War, Churchill was captured by Boer forces after an armored train ambush.","details":null,"id":"805","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Captured During Boer War","year":"1899"},{"description":"Churchill made a daring escape from captivity, becoming a national hero throughout Britain.","details":null,"id":"806","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Escaped Boer Captivity","year":"1899"},{"description":"Churchill was elected Conservative Member of Parliament for Oldham, beginning his long parliamentary career.","details":null,"id":"807","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Elected to Parliament","year":"1900"},{"description":"Disagreeing with Conservative trade policies, Churchill crossed the floor to join the Liberal Party.","details":null,"id":"808","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Joined Liberal Party","year":"1904"},{"description":"Churchill received his first government appointment as Under-Secretary of State for the Colonies.","details":null,"id":"809","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Under-Secretary for the Colonies","year":"1905"},{"description":"Churchill introduced labor exchanges and social welfare reforms aimed at reducing unemployment and improving workers' rights.","details":null,"id":"810","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"President of the Board of Trade","year":"1908"},{"description":"Churchill married Clementine Hozier, whose support became an important influence throughout his personal and political life.","details":null,"id":"811","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Married Clementine Hozier","year":"1908"},{"description":"Churchill became Home Secretary, overseeing prison reforms, policing, and responses to industrial unrest across Britain.","details":null,"id":"812","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Home Secretary","year":"1910"},{"description":"Churchill was appointed First Lord of the Admiralty, modernizing the Royal Navy before the outbreak of the First World War.","details":null,"id":"813","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"First Lord of the Admiralty","year":"1911"},{"description":"As First Lord of the Admiralty, Churchill helped mobilize the Royal Navy immediately after Britain declared war on Germany.","details":null,"id":"814","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Britain Entered World War I","year":"1914"},{"description":"The Gallipoli campaign failed with heavy Allied casualties, damaging Churchill's political reputation and forcing his resignation from the Admiralty.","details":null,"id":"815","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Gallipoli Campaign","year":"1915"},{"description":"Churchill left the Admiralty following criticism over Gallipoli and accepted a reduced government role.","details":null,"id":"816","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Resigned from Admiralty","year":"1915"},{"description":"Churchill commanded the 6th Battalion, Royal Scots Fusiliers, on the Western Front.","details":null,"id":"817","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Returned to Army","year":"1916"},{"description":"Returned to government and oversaw Britain's wartime weapons production.","details":null,"id":"818","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Minister of Munitions","year":"1917"},{"description":"Managed postwar military affairs and supported intervention during the Russian Civil War.","details":null,"id":"819","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Secretary of State for War","year":"1919"},{"description":"Oversaw British colonial policy and the Irish settlement negotiations.","details":null,"id":"820","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Colonial Secretary","year":"1921"},{"description":"Lost his Dundee seat in the general election.","details":null,"id":"821","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Lost Parliamentary Seat","year":"1922"},{"description":"Returned as Conservative MP for Epping.","details":null,"id":"822","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Returned to Parliament","year":"1924"},{"description":"Appointed Chancellor, overseeing Britain's financial policy.","details":null,"id":"823","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Chancellor of the Exchequer","year":"1924"},{"description":"Britain returned to the Gold Standard, a decision later widely criticized.","details":null,"id":"824","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Gold Standard Restored","year":"1925"},{"description":"Left government after the general election.","details":null,"id":"825","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Conservatives Defeated","year":"1929"},{"description":"Spent years outside government warning against German rearmament.","details":null,"id":"826","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Wilderness Years Began","year":"1930"},{"description":"His stance on India generated significant controversy.","details":null,"id":"827","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Opposed Indian Self-Government","year":"1931"},{"description":"Repeatedly urged Britain to strengthen defenses against Nazi Germany.","details":null,"id":"828","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Warned About Hitler","year":"1935"},{"description":"Criticized appeasement, warning it would encourage Hitler.","details":null,"id":"829","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Opposed Munich Agreement","year":"1938"},{"description":"Reappointed First Lord of the Admiralty after war began.","details":null,"id":"830","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Returned to Admiralty","year":"1939"},{"description":"Succeeded Neville Chamberlain as Prime Minister during Britain's greatest crisis.","details":null,"id":"831","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Became Prime Minister","year":"1940"},{"description":"His speeches inspired Britain during victory in the Battle of Britain.","details":null,"id":"832","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Battle of Britain","year":"1940"},{"description":"Met Franklin D. Roosevelt to establish shared Allied war aims.","details":null,"id":"833","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Atlantic Charter","year":"1941"},{"description":"Churchill strengthened Allied cooperation while directing Britain's wartime strategy during some of the conflict's most challenging years.","details":null,"id":"834","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Leadership During World War II","year":"1942"},{"description":"Met Allied leaders to coordinate military strategy and agree on demanding the Axis powers' unconditional surrender.","details":null,"id":"835","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Casablanca Conference","year":"1943"},{"description":"Met Roosevelt and Stalin to coordinate plans for defeating Nazi Germany and opening a Western Front.","details":null,"id":"836","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Tehran Conference","year":"1943"},{"description":"Played a major role in planning and supporting the Allied invasion of Normandy.","details":null,"id":"837","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Supported D-Day","year":"1944"},{"description":"Worked closely with Allied leaders as German occupation ended across much of Western Europe.","details":null,"id":"838","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Liberation of Western Europe","year":"1944"},{"description":"Joined Roosevelt and Stalin to discuss the postwar order and the future of Europe.","details":null,"id":"839","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Yalta Conference","year":"1945"},{"description":"Announced Germany's surrender and celebrated Victory in Europe Day with the British public.","details":null,"id":"840","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Victory in Europe","year":"1945"},{"description":"Despite wartime leadership, Churchill's Conservative Party lost the general election.","details":null,"id":"841","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Election Defeat","year":"1945"},{"description":"Delivered the famous 'Iron Curtain' speech, warning of growing Soviet influence across Eastern Europe.","details":null,"id":"842","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Iron Curtain Speech","year":"1946"},{"description":"Won the general election and began his second term as Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"843","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Returned as Prime Minister","year":"1951"},{"description":"Received the Order of the Garter, Britain's highest order of chivalry.","details":null,"id":"844","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Knighted","year":"1953"},{"description":"Awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature for his historical writings and exceptional oratory.","details":null,"id":"845","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Nobel Prize in Literature","year":"1953"},{"description":"Suffered a serious stroke but initially continued serving as Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"846","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Stroke","year":"1953"},{"description":"Retired as Prime Minister after serving Britain through two separate terms.","details":null,"id":"847","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Resigned as Prime Minister","year":"1955"},{"description":"Became the first honorary citizen of the United States.","details":null,"id":"848","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Honorary U.S. Citizen","year":"1963"},{"description":"Churchill died in London at the age of 90 after a distinguished public career.","details":null,"id":"849","side":"negative","timeline_id":"44","title":"Death","year":"1965"},{"description":"Received a state funeral attended by world leaders, honoring his extraordinary service.","details":null,"id":"850","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"State Funeral","year":"1965"},{"description":"Remembered as one of Britain's greatest wartime leaders and an influential twentieth-century statesman.","details":null,"id":"851","side":"positive","timeline_id":"44","title":"Enduring Legacy","year":"1965"},{"description":"Jawaharlal Nehru was born on 14 November 1889 in Allahabad into the prominent Nehru family.","details":null,"id":"852","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Born","year":"1889"},{"description":"Began studies at Harrow School in England, receiving a British-style education.","details":null,"id":"853","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Harrow School","year":"1905"},{"description":"Entered Trinity College, Cambridge, to study natural sciences.","details":null,"id":"854","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Trinity College","year":"1907"},{"description":"Started legal studies at the Inner Temple in London.","details":null,"id":"855","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Legal Training","year":"1910"},{"description":"Qualified as a barrister and returned to India to practice law.","details":null,"id":"856","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Called to the Bar","year":"1912"},{"description":"Attended his first Indian National Congress session, beginning political involvement.","details":null,"id":"857","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Congress Session","year":"1912"},{"description":"Married Kamala Kaul; their daughter Indira was born the following year.","details":null,"id":"858","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Married Kamala Kaul","year":"1916"},{"description":"Met Mahatma Gandhi, beginning a lifelong political association.","details":null,"id":"859","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Met Mahatma Gandhi","year":"1916"},{"description":"Supported the Home Rule Movement seeking greater self-government for India.","details":null,"id":"860","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Home Rule Movement","year":"1917"},{"description":"The massacre strengthened Nehru's commitment to India's independence movement.","details":null,"id":"861","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Jallianwala Bagh Aftermath","year":"1919"},{"description":"Joined Gandhi's Non-Cooperation Movement against British rule.","details":null,"id":"862","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Non-Cooperation Movement","year":"1920"},{"description":"Arrested for participating in the freedom movement.","details":null,"id":"863","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"First Imprisonment","year":"1921"},{"description":"Became General Secretary of the Indian National Congress.","details":null,"id":"864","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Congress General Secretary","year":"1923"},{"description":"Attended the Congress of Oppressed Nationalities in Brussels, expanding international contacts.","details":null,"id":"865","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"International Congress","year":"1927"},{"description":"Advocated complete independence as political demands intensified.","details":null,"id":"866","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Nehru Report Debate","year":"1928"},{"description":"Elected President of the Indian National Congress at the Lahore Session.","details":null,"id":"867","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Congress President","year":"1929"},{"description":"Congress adopted Complete Independence as its national objective.","details":null,"id":"868","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Purna Swaraj Resolution","year":"1929"},{"description":"Played a leading role in the Civil Disobedience Movement and was imprisoned.","details":null,"id":"869","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Civil Disobedience","year":"1930"},{"description":"Released following the Gandhi-Irwin Pact.","details":null,"id":"870","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Released from Prison","year":"1931"},{"description":"Published 'An Autobiography', reflecting on his life and India's freedom struggle.","details":null,"id":"871","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Autobiography Published","year":"1934"},{"description":"Criticized the Government of India Act while continuing to campaign for full independence.","details":null,"id":"872","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Government of India Act Debate","year":"1935"},{"description":"Elected President of the Indian National Congress and emphasized socialist economic ideas.","details":null,"id":"873","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Congress President Again","year":"1936"},{"description":"His wife Kamala Nehru died after a prolonged illness.","details":null,"id":"874","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Death of Kamala Nehru","year":"1936"},{"description":"Campaigned extensively as Congress formed governments in several provinces.","details":null,"id":"875","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Provincial Elections","year":"1937"},{"description":"Established the National Planning Committee to study India's economic development.","details":null,"id":"876","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"National Planning Committee","year":"1938"},{"description":"Opposed India's automatic entry into the war without Indian consent.","details":null,"id":"877","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Second World War Begins","year":"1939"},{"description":"Imprisoned for anti-colonial political activities during the freedom movement.","details":null,"id":"878","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Arrested","year":"1940"},{"description":"Joined the Quit India Movement demanding immediate British withdrawal.","details":null,"id":"879","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Quit India Movement","year":"1942"},{"description":"Arrested after the Quit India Movement and remained imprisoned until 1945.","details":null,"id":"880","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Longest Imprisonment","year":"1942"},{"description":"Released as World War II ended and independence negotiations resumed.","details":null,"id":"881","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Released from Prison","year":"1945"},{"description":"Assumed leadership of Congress during the transfer of power negotiations.","details":null,"id":"882","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Congress President","year":"1946"},{"description":"Became Vice President of the Interim Government of India.","details":null,"id":"883","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Interim Government","year":"1946"},{"description":"India became independent on 15 August 1947.","details":null,"id":"884","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"India's Independence","year":"1947"},{"description":"Became the first Prime Minister of independent India.","details":null,"id":"885","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"First Prime Minister","year":"1947"},{"description":"India's partition caused widespread communal violence and displacement.","details":null,"id":"886","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Partition Violence","year":"1947"},{"description":"Worked to preserve national unity after Gandhi's assassination.","details":null,"id":"887","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Death of Mahatma Gandhi","year":"1948"},{"description":"Led India's response during the first Indo-Pakistani conflict over Kashmir.","details":null,"id":"888","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Kashmir Conflict","year":"1948"},{"description":"India remained a member of the Commonwealth as a republic.","details":null,"id":"889","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Commonwealth Membership","year":"1949"},{"description":"Oversaw India's transition into a sovereign democratic republic.","details":null,"id":"890","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Republic of India","year":"1950"},{"description":"Launched India's first Five-Year Plan focused on agriculture and development.","details":null,"id":"891","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"First Five-Year Plan","year":"1951"},{"description":"Led the Indian National Congress to victory in India's first general election under universal adult franchise.","details":null,"id":"892","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"First General Election","year":"1952"},{"description":"Initiated efforts that eventually led to linguistic reorganization of Indian states.","details":null,"id":"893","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"States Reorganisation Begins","year":"1953"},{"description":"Signed the Panchsheel Agreement with China promoting peaceful coexistence.","details":null,"id":"894","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Panchsheel Agreement","year":"1954"},{"description":"Played a leading role in the Asian-African Conference at Bandung.","details":null,"id":"895","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Bandung Conference","year":"1955"},{"description":"Awarded India's highest civilian honor, the Bharat Ratna.","details":null,"id":"896","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Bharat Ratna","year":"1955"},{"description":"Oversaw implementation of the States Reorganisation Act.","details":null,"id":"897","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"States Reorganisation Act","year":"1956"},{"description":"Won a second consecutive national election as Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"898","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Second General Election","year":"1957"},{"description":"India granted asylum to the 14th Dalai Lama after he fled Tibet.","details":null,"id":"899","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Dalai Lama Granted Asylum","year":"1959"},{"description":"Signed the Indus Waters Treaty with Pakistan through World Bank mediation.","details":null,"id":"900","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Indus Waters Treaty","year":"1960"},{"description":"Indian armed forces integrated Goa into the Indian Union.","details":null,"id":"901","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Liberation of Goa","year":"1961"},{"description":"Helped shape the emerging Non-Aligned Movement with other world leaders.","details":null,"id":"902","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Non-Aligned Movement","year":"1961"},{"description":"Secured another electoral victory and continued as Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"903","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Third General Election","year":"1962"},{"description":"India suffered a military defeat during the border conflict with China.","details":null,"id":"904","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Sino-Indian War","year":"1962"},{"description":"Implemented organizational reforms within the Indian National Congress.","details":null,"id":"905","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Kamaraj Plan","year":"1963"},{"description":"His health deteriorated following the strain of the China conflict.","details":null,"id":"906","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Health Declined","year":"1963"},{"description":"Continued performing official duties despite declining health.","details":null,"id":"907","side":"positive","timeline_id":"45","title":"Final Public Appearance","year":"1964"},{"description":"Jawaharlal Nehru died on 27 May 1964 while serving as Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"908","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"Death","year":"1964"},{"description":"India observed widespread mourning following the death of its first Prime Minister.","details":null,"id":"909","side":"negative","timeline_id":"45","title":"National Mourning","year":"1964"},{"description":"Vladimir Vladimirovich Putin was born on 7 October 1952 in Leningrad, Soviet Union.","details":null,"id":"910","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Born","year":"1952"},{"description":"Began formal schooling in Leningrad and developed an interest in sports and academics.","details":null,"id":"911","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Primary Education","year":"1960"},{"description":"Took up sambo and judo, eventually earning advanced ranks.","details":null,"id":"912","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Started Judo","year":"1964"},{"description":"Studied law at Leningrad State University.","details":null,"id":"913","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Entered Leningrad State University","year":"1970"},{"description":"Graduated with a law degree and joined the KGB.","details":null,"id":"914","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Graduated in Law","year":"1975"},{"description":"Began his career as an intelligence officer in the Soviet security service.","details":null,"id":"915","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Joined KGB","year":"1975"},{"description":"Married Lyudmila Shkrebneva; the couple later had two daughters.","details":null,"id":"916","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Married Lyudmila","year":"1983"},{"description":"Served as a KGB officer in Dresden, East Germany.","details":null,"id":"917","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Posted to Dresden","year":"1985"},{"description":"Returned from East Germany as the Soviet bloc collapsed.","details":null,"id":"918","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Returned to Leningrad","year":"1990"},{"description":"Worked as an adviser at Leningrad State University.","details":null,"id":"919","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"University Adviser","year":"1990"},{"description":"Left active KGB service during the Soviet Union's final months.","details":null,"id":"920","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Resigned from KGB","year":"1991"},{"description":"Joined Mayor Anatoly Sobchak's administration.","details":null,"id":"921","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Saint Petersburg Administration","year":"1991"},{"description":"Became First Deputy Mayor of Saint Petersburg.","details":null,"id":"922","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Deputy Mayor","year":"1994"},{"description":"Moved to Moscow to work in the Presidential Administration.","details":null,"id":"923","side":"positive","timeline_id":"46","title":"Moved to Moscow","year":"1996"},{"description":"Advanced to senior positions in the Kremlin administration.","details":null,"id":"9