":null,"id":"3476","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"ODI Century Record","year":"2023"},{"description":"Kohli and Anushka Sharma welcomed their son Akaay.","details":null,"id":"3477","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"Birth of Son","year":"2024"},{"description":"Kohli was named Player of the Match in the final as India defeated South Africa to win the 2024 ICC Men's T20 World Cup.","details":null,"id":"3478","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"T20 World Cup Victory","year":"29 Jun 2024"},{"description":"Kohli announced his retirement from Twenty20 International cricket after India's World Cup victory.","details":null,"id":"3479","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"T20I Retirement","year":"29 Jun 2024"},{"description":"Kohli continued developing fitness, apparel, restaurant, and sports-business ventures, including partnerships associated with One8.","details":null,"id":"3480","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"Entrepreneurship and Brand Ventures","year":"2024"},{"description":"Kohli announced his retirement from Test cricket after an internationally significant red-ball career.","details":null,"id":"3481","side":"negative","timeline_id":"117","title":"Test Retirement","year":"2025"},{"description":"He remained available for India's ODI cricket while continuing his commercial and philanthropic activities.","details":null,"id":"3482","side":"positive","timeline_id":"117","title":"ODI Career Continuation","year":"2025"},{"description":"Rafael Nadal Parera was born in Manacor, Mallorca, Spain.","details":null,"id":"3483","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Birth","year":"3 Jun 1986"},{"description":"Nadal began playing tennis as a young child under the guidance of his uncle and coach Toni Nadal.","details":null,"id":"3484","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Started Playing Tennis","year":"1991"},{"description":"Nadal won national junior titles and emerged as one of Spain's most promising young tennis players.","details":null,"id":"3485","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Spanish Junior Success","year":"1998"},{"description":"He began competing on the professional circuit as a teenager.","details":null,"id":"3486","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Professional Transition","year":"2001"},{"description":"Nadal won his first ATP-level match at the Mallorca Open and became one of the youngest players to win an ATP match.","details":null,"id":"3487","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"ATP-Level Victory","year":"2002"},{"description":"He reached his first ATP tournament quarterfinal in Auckland.","details":null,"id":"3488","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"First ATP Tournament Quarterfinal","year":"2003"},{"description":"Nadal made his Wimbledon debut and became one of the youngest men to win a match at the tournament.","details":null,"id":"3489","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wimbledon Debut","year":"2003"},{"description":"Nadal won his first ATP singles title in Sopot, Poland.","details":null,"id":"3490","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"First ATP Title","year":"2004"},{"description":"He helped Spain win the Davis Cup and became a key member of the national team.","details":null,"id":"3491","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Davis Cup Victory","year":"2004"},{"description":"Nadal won the French Open on his debut at Roland-Garros.","details":null,"id":"3492","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"First French Open Victory","year":"2005"},{"description":"His clay-court dominance lifted him into the top five of the ATP rankings.","details":null,"id":"3493","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"First Top-Five Ranking","year":"2005"},{"description":"Nadal received major year-end recognition after winning multiple titles and establishing himself as a leading player.","details":null,"id":"3494","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"ATP Player of the Year","year":"2005"},{"description":"He successfully defended his French Open title.","details":null,"id":"3495","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Second French Open Victory","year":"2006"},{"description":"Nadal won his third consecutive French Open championship.","details":null,"id":"3496","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Third French Open Victory","year":"2007"},{"description":"He won the French Open for the fourth straight year.","details":null,"id":"3497","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Fourth French Open Victory","year":"2008"},{"description":"Nadal defeated Roger Federer in a historic Wimbledon final to win his first Wimbledon title.","details":null,"id":"3498","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"First Wimbledon Victory","year":"2008"},{"description":"Nadal became the world number-one men's singles player for the first time.","details":null,"id":"3499","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"World Number One","year":"18 Aug 2008"},{"description":"He won the men's singles gold medal at the Beijing Olympics.","details":null,"id":"3500","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Olympic Singles Gold","year":"2008"},{"description":"Nadal won his first Australian Open title after defeating Federer in the final.","details":null,"id":"3501","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Australian Open Victory","year":"2009"},{"description":"Knee problems contributed to Nadal's defeat at the French Open and his withdrawal from Wimbledon.","details":null,"id":"3502","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Knee Injury and French Open Loss","year":"2009"},{"description":"Nadal withdrew from Wimbledon because of knee tendinitis, ending his title defense.","details":null,"id":"3503","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wimbledon Withdrawal","year":"2009"},{"description":"Nadal won Wimbledon after returning from his injury-related absence.","details":null,"id":"3504","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Second Wimbledon Victory","year":"2010"},{"description":"He won the US Open for the first time and completed the career Grand Slam.","details":null,"id":"3505","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"US Open Victory","year":"2010"},{"description":"Nadal became the youngest man in the Open Era to complete the singles career Grand Slam.","details":null,"id":"3506","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Career Grand Slam","year":"2010"},{"description":"He defeated Federer in the final to win his sixth French Open title.","details":null,"id":"3507","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Sixth French Open Victory","year":"2011"},{"description":"Nadal became the tournament's record men's singles champion at that time by winning his seventh Roland-Garros title.","details":null,"id":"3508","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Seventh French Open Victory","year":"2012"},{"description":"A knee injury forced Nadal to withdraw from the 2012 Wimbledon Championships.","details":null,"id":"3509","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wimbledon Withdrawal","year":"2012"},{"description":"Nadal returned after a lengthy knee-related absence and quickly regained elite form.","details":null,"id":"3510","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Return From Injury","year":"2013"},{"description":"He won his eighth French Open title.","details":null,"id":"3511","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Eighth French Open Victory","year":"2013"},{"description":"Nadal won his second US Open championship.","details":null,"id":"3512","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Second US Open Victory","year":"2013"},{"description":"He won his ninth French Open title and continued his unprecedented dominance on clay.","details":null,"id":"3513","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Ninth French Open Victory","year":"2014"},{"description":"A right-wrist injury forced Nadal to miss the North American hard-court swing and affected his preparation for the US Open.","details":null,"id":"3514","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wrist Injury","year":"2014"},{"description":"Injuries and inconsistent form caused Nadal to fall outside the world's top five for the first time in many years.","details":null,"id":"3515","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Ranking Decline","year":"2015"},{"description":"Nadal won the men's doubles gold medal at the Rio Olympics with Marc López.","details":null,"id":"3516","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Olympic Doubles Gold","year":"2016"},{"description":"A left-wrist injury forced him to withdraw from the French Open and miss Wimbledon.","details":null,"id":"3517","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wrist Injury Withdrawal","year":"2016"},{"description":"Nadal became the first man to win ten titles at a single Grand Slam tournament by claiming La Décima at Roland-Garros.","details":null,"id":"3518","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Tenth French Open Victory","year":"2017"},{"description":"He won his third US Open championship.","details":null,"id":"3519","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Third US Open Victory","year":"2017"},{"description":"Nadal won his eleventh French Open title.","details":null,"id":"3520","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Eleventh French Open Victory","year":"2018"},{"description":"He won a record-extending twelfth French Open championship.","details":null,"id":"3521","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Twelfth French Open Victory","year":"2019"},{"description":"Nadal won his fourth US Open title.","details":null,"id":"3522","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Fourth US Open Victory","year":"2019"},{"description":"He won the French Open for the thirteenth time and equaled Roger Federer's then-record of 20 men's Grand Slam singles titles.","details":null,"id":"3523","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Thirteenth French Open Victory","year":"2020"},{"description":"A chronic left-foot injury caused Nadal to miss much of the season, including Wimbledon and the US Open.","details":null,"id":"3524","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Foot Injury","year":"2021"},{"description":"Nadal won the Australian Open for the second time and claimed his 21st Grand Slam singles title.","details":null,"id":"3525","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Australian Open Victory","year":"2022"},{"description":"He won his fourteenth French Open title despite playing with severe foot pain.","details":null,"id":"3526","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Fourteenth French Open Victory","year":"2022"},{"description":"Nadal withdrew from the Wimbledon semi-final because of an abdominal tear.","details":null,"id":"3527","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Wimbledon Withdrawal","year":"2022"},{"description":"He sustained a hip injury at the Australian Open and missed most of the 2023 season.","details":null,"id":"3528","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Hip Injury","year":"2023"},{"description":"Nadal indicated that 2024 might be his final season because of continuing physical problems.","details":null,"id":"3529","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Retirement Possibility Announced","year":"2023"},{"description":"He returned to competitive tennis at the Brisbane International after a year-long injury absence.","details":null,"id":"3530","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Return to Competition","year":"2024"},{"description":"Nadal competed at Roland-Garros but lost in the first round, a rare early exit at his most successful tournament.","details":null,"id":"3531","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Final French Open Appearance","year":"2024"},{"description":"He competed at the Paris Olympics in singles and doubles, partnering with Carlos Alcaraz in doubles.","details":null,"id":"3532","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Olympic Appearance","year":"2024"},{"description":"Nadal announced that he would retire from professional tennis after the Davis Cup Finals.","details":null,"id":"3533","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Retirement Announcement","year":"10 Oct 2024"},{"description":"He played his final professional match for Spain against the Netherlands in the Davis Cup Finals.","details":null,"id":"3534","side":"negative","timeline_id":"118","title":"Final Professional Match","year":"19 Nov 2024"},{"description":"After retirement, Nadal continued developing his tennis academy, foundation, and sports-related business interests.","details":null,"id":"3535","side":"positive","timeline_id":"118","title":"Rafa Nadal Academy","year":"2025"},{"description":"Manan Kumar Mishra was born in Bihar. Public sources variously identify his birthplace as Gopalganj district or Bagaha, so the precise birthplace is not consistently reported.","details":null,"id":"3536","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Born In Bihar","year":"01 Nov 1956"},{"description":"He began studying for a Bachelor of Science degree at Rajendra College, Chapra, then affiliated with Bihar University.","details":null,"id":"3537","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Began Science Degree","year":"1973"},{"description":"He completed a BSc Honours degree from Rajendra College, Chapra, according to election-affidavit information.","details":null,"id":"3538","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Completed BSc Honours","year":"1976"},{"description":"He began pursuing a professional Bachelor of Laws degree at Patna Law College, Patna University.","details":null,"id":"3539","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Started Legal Studies","year":"1977"},{"description":"He completed his LLB from Patna Law College, Patna University. Public biographies report that he was the topper and gold medalist of his batch.","details":null,"id":"3540","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Earned Law Degree","year":"1980"},{"description":"After completing his legal education, he began practising as an advocate at the Gopalganj Civil Court in Bihar.","details":null,"id":"3541","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Started Court Practice","year":"1980"},{"description":"He began practising law at the Patna High Court, marking his transition from district-court practice to a higher court.","details":null,"id":"3542","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Joined Patna High Court","year":"1982"},{"description":"He was elected as a member of the Bihar State Bar Council.","details":null,"id":"3543","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Joined Bihar Bar Council","year":"1989"},{"description":"He was designated as a senior advocate, reflecting recognition of his legal experience and standing.","details":null,"id":"3544","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Designated Senior Advocate","year":"2007"},{"description":"He shifted his legal practice from the Patna High Court to the Supreme Court of India.","details":null,"id":"3545","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Moved To Supreme Court","year":"2009"},{"description":"He contested the 2010 Bihar Legislative Assembly election as a candidate of the Indian National Congress.","details":null,"id":"3546","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Entered Bihar Politics","year":"2010"},{"description":"He was elected as a representative of the Bihar State Bar Council to the Bar Council of India.","details":null,"id":"3547","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Joined Bar Council","year":"2010"},{"description":"He was elected chairman of the Bar Council of India for the first time.","details":null,"id":"3548","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"First Led BCI","year":"17 Apr 2012"},{"description":"He was again chosen as chairman of the Bar Council of India.","details":null,"id":"3549","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Returned As BCI Chairman","year":"09 Nov 2014"},{"description":"He continued appearing as a senior advocate before the Supreme Court while participating in Bar Council affairs. His work increasingly combined Supreme Court advocacy with responsibilities concerning legal education and professional regulation.","details":null,"id":"3552","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Advanced Legal Representation","year":"2017"},{"description":"He continued participating in the regulation of legal education, enrolment, and professional standards through the Bar Council of India.","details":null,"id":"3556","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Maintained BCI Leadership","year":"2021"},{"description":"The Bharatiya Janata Party nominated him as a Rajya Sabha candidate from Bihar.","details":null,"id":"3559","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Nominated For Rajya Sabha","year":"20 Aug 2024"},{"description":"He was elected unopposed to the Rajya Sabha from Bihar after being nominated by the BJP.","details":null,"id":"3560","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Elected Unopposed","year":"Aug 2024"},{"description":"His Rajya Sabha election marked a transition from primarily legal-profession leadership into national parliamentary politics.","details":null,"id":"3561","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Joined Parliamentary Politics","year":"2024"},{"description":"He was reported to have been elected chairman of the Bar Council of India for a seventh consecutive term.","details":null,"id":"3562","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Won Seventh BCI Term","year":"2025"},{"description":"As BCI chairman, he faced controversy after an order concerning the enrolment of NALSAR law graduates following a student protest linked to a proposed Chief Justice of India visit.","details":null,"id":"3563","side":"negative","timeline_id":"119","title":"Faced NALSAR Controversy","year":"13 Aug 2026"},{"description":"The Bar Council leadership reconsidered and withdrew the enrolment-related order, stating that most students were not responsible and awaiting an inquiry report.","details":null,"id":"3564","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Retracted NALSAR Order","year":"13 Aug 2026"},{"description":"As of August 2026, he was publicly reported as chairman of the Bar Council of India and a BJP member of the Rajya Sabha.","details":null,"id":"3565","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Served As BCI Chairman","year":"15 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Manan Kumar Mishra’s self-declared criminal, educational, income, assets, and liabilities information from his Rajya Sabha election affidavit is available through the MyNeta database: [Rajya Sabha election affidavit Link](https://www.myneta.info/rajsab09aff/candidate.php?candidate_id=1107)","details":null,"id":"3566","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Rajya Sabha election affidavit","year":"Aug 2024"},{"description":"The attached thread reports that, while serving as Chairman of the Bar Council of India, Manan Kumar Mishra publicly campaigned for Narendra Modi in Varanasi and spoke in support of him at a BCI event in Gandhinagar.","details":null,"id":"3567","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Campaigned For Modi","year":"2014"},{"description":"As stated in a BCI document signed by Manan Kumar Mishra, the Bar Council of India forwarded draft rules for the registration and regulation of foreign lawyers and foreign law firms in India to the Union Law Minister.","details":null,"id":"3568","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Submitted Foreign-Lawyer Rules","year":"31 May 2016"},{"description":"As Chairman of the Bar Council of India, Manan Kumar Mishra issued a press release arguing that retired judges should observe a cooling-off period before accepting government appointments to help protect judicial independence.","details":null,"id":"3569","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Issued Judicial Independence Statement","year":"29 Sep 2018"},{"description":"The Bar Council of India, under Manan Kumar Mishra’s chairmanship, welcomed former Chief Justice of India Ranjan Gogoi’s nomination to the Rajya Sabha and described it as a bridge between the judiciary and legislature.","details":null,"id":"3570","side":"positive","timeline_id":"119","title":"Welcomed Gogoi Nomination","year":"18 Mar 2020"},{"description":"The attached thread reports that Bar Council rules restricting public criticism of the BCI and State Bar Councils drew substantial backlash and that the disputed provisions were later kept in abeyance.","details":null,"id":"3571","side":"negative","timeline_id":"119","title":"Faced Criticism Over Rules","year":"2021"},{"description":"Ram Kisan Yadav, later known as Baba Ramdev, was born in Said Alipur village in Mahendragarh district, Haryana, to farmer parents Ram Niwas Yadav and Gulabo Devi.","details":null,"id":"3572","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Born In Haryana","year":"25 Dec 1965"},{"description":"Ramdev has said that he experienced paralysis or severe physical illness during childhood and later attributed his recovery to yoga practice.","details":null,"id":"3573","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Experienced Childhood Illness","year":"1970s"},{"description":"He attended a government school in or near Shahjadpur and studied through approximately the eighth standard.","details":null,"id":"3574","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Studied At Village School","year":"1970s"},{"description":"After his early schooling, he joined traditional gurukuls to study Sanskrit, Indian scriptures, and yoga.","details":null,"id":"3575","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Entered Gurukul Education","year":"1980s"},{"description":"At Gurukul Kalwa in Jind district, Haryana, he studied under Acharya Baldev and developed expertise in Sanskrit, yoga, and traditional Indian philosophy.","details":null,"id":"3576","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Studied At Gurukul Kalwa","year":"1980s"},{"description":"He received yoga training associated with Arya Samaj teachers, including Guru Karanvir, during his gurukul years.","details":null,"id":"3577","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Learned Yogic Practices","year":"1980s"},{"description":"During his traditional education, Ramdev met Balkrishna, who later became his principal collaborator in building the Patanjali group.","details":null,"id":"3578","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Met Acharya Balkrishna","year":"1980s"},{"description":"While associated with Gurukul Kalwa, he began offering free yoga instruction to villagers in Haryana.","details":null,"id":"3579","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Taught Villagers Yoga","year":"1980s"},{"description":"Ramdev took sannyas initiation and adopted the name Swami Ramdev, committing himself to yoga, spiritual practice, and celibacy.","details":null,"id":"3580","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Adopted Ascetic Life","year":"1990s"},{"description":"He moved to Haridwar, Uttarakhand, where he undertook meditation, self-discipline, and study of Indian religious and philosophical texts.","details":null,"id":"3581","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Moved To Haridwar","year":"1990s"},{"description":"He spent several years studying ancient Indian scriptures and related subjects at Gurukul Kangri Vishwavidyalaya in Haridwar.","details":null,"id":"3582","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Studied At Gurukul Kangri","year":"1990s"},{"description":"Ramdev and Balkrishna established the Divya Yog Mandir Trust at Kripalu Bagh Ashram in Haridwar to promote yoga and Ayurveda.","details":null,"id":"3583","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Founded Divya Yog Mandir","year":"05 Jan 1995"},{"description":"He conducted yoga classes and camps in India, combining traditional practices with accessible public instruction.","details":null,"id":"3584","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Expanded Yoga Teaching","year":"1990s"},{"description":"Ramdev’s yoga instruction began reaching a much larger audience through televised appearances and recorded yoga programming.","details":null,"id":"3585","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Began Television Outreach","year":"2002"},{"description":"Aastha TV began broadcasting his yoga camps, making him a nationally recognized yoga teacher and significantly expanding his following.","details":null,"id":"3586","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Joined Aastha Television","year":"2003"},{"description":"Televised morning yoga sessions helped Ramdev reach millions of viewers and established his public image as a mass yoga instructor.","details":null,"id":"3587","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Built National Following","year":"2003"},{"description":"Workers associated with the Divya Yog Mandir Trust raised issues concerning wages and employee benefits; the dispute led to negotiations and public criticism.","details":null,"id":"3588","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Faced Labour Dispute","year":"2005"},{"description":"Ramdev and Balkrishna established Patanjali Yogpeeth in Haridwar as an institution for yoga, Ayurveda, research, and education.","details":null,"id":"3589","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Founded Patanjali Yogpeeth","year":"2006"},{"description":"Ramdev and Balkrishna co-founded Patanjali Ayurved to manufacture and market Ayurvedic, personal-care, food, and consumer products.","details":null,"id":"3590","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Co-founded Patanjali Ayurved","year":"2006"},{"description":"He publicly promoted yoga education as an alternative or complement to aspects of modern health and sex education, generating debate.","details":null,"id":"3591","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Advocated Yoga Education","year":"2006"},{"description":"Ramdev began taking a more visible role in public campaigns involving corruption, black money, national identity, and economic self-reliance.","details":null,"id":"3592","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Entered Public Activism","year":"2006"},{"description":"Patanjali-linked institutions broadened activities in Ayurvedic treatment, pharmaceutical production, education, and yoga research.","details":null,"id":"3593","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Expanded Ayurvedic Institutions","year":"2007"},{"description":"He conducted yoga programs and lectures outside India, including appearances and teaching activities in countries such as the United States, United Kingdom, and Japan.","details":null,"id":"3594","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Reached International Audiences","year":"2008"},{"description":"Patanjali expanded its consumer-products portfolio, including Ayurvedic medicines, food items, personal-care products, and household goods.","details":null,"id":"3595","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Launched Consumer Products","year":"2009"},{"description":"Ramdev increasingly marketed Patanjali products as Indian and Ayurvedic alternatives to multinational consumer brands.","details":null,"id":"3596","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Promoted Swadeshi Products","year":"2010"},{"description":"He began a major public fast and protest at New Delhi’s Ramlila Maidan demanding action against corruption and unaccounted wealth held abroad.","details":null,"id":"3597","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Started Black-Money Protest","year":"04 Jun 2011"},{"description":"Police removed protesters from Ramlila Maidan during the night, and Ramdev left the site in disguise; the crackdown became a major controversy.","details":null,"id":"3598","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Police Ended Protest","year":"05 Jun 2011"},{"description":"He promoted the Bharat Swabhiman movement and trust, which advocated anti-corruption measures, economic nationalism, and political reform.","details":null,"id":"3599","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Formed Bharat Swabhiman","year":"2011"},{"description":"He was reportedly detained for several hours at London’s Heathrow Airport, an incident that attracted media attention but did not end his international activities.","details":null,"id":"3601","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Detained At Heathrow","year":"2013"},{"description":"Ramdev publicly supported the Bharatiya Janata Party and Narendra Modi during India’s 2014 general-election campaign.","details":null,"id":"3602","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Supported BJP Campaign","year":"2014"},{"description":"The Haryana government appointed him as a brand ambassador for yoga and Ayurveda.","details":null,"id":"3603","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Named Haryana Yoga Ambassador","year":"2015"},{"description":"Ramdev declined the proposed Padma Vibhushan recognition, saying that he preferred recognition for his work rather than a government award.","details":null,"id":"3604","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Declined Padma Honour","year":"2015"},{"description":"Patanjali’s rapid growth in food, personal care, and household products made it a major challenger to established Indian and multinational FMCG companies.","details":null,"id":"3605","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Patanjali Challenged Established Brands","year":"2016"},{"description":"Patanjali faced action and penalties connected with allegations that some advertisements made misleading or exaggerated product claims.","details":null,"id":"3606","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Faced Advertising Penalty","year":"2016"},{"description":"Patanjali continued investing in manufacturing, distribution, food processing, and agricultural supply chains across India.","details":null,"id":"3607","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Expanded Manufacturing Network","year":"2017"},{"description":"Patanjali acquired debt-laden edible-oil company Ruchi Soya Industries through an insolvency-resolution process, expanding its presence in edible oils and food products.","details":null,"id":"3608","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Acquired Ruchi Soya","year":"2018"},{"description":"Ruchi Soya was subsequently rebranded as Patanjali Foods, strengthening the group’s position in the packaged-food and edible-oil markets.","details":null,"id":"3609","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Rebranded Ruchi Soya","year":"2019"},{"description":"Patanjali launched Coronil and related products while presenting them as treatments for COVID-19, prompting criticism from medical bodies and regulatory authorities over the claims.","details":null,"id":"3610","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Launched Coronil Product","year":"2020"},{"description":"Authorities and medical organizations challenged the presentation and promotion of Coronil as a COVID-19 remedy, leading to legal and regulatory scrutiny.","details":null,"id":"3611","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Faced COVID Claims Dispute","year":"2020"},{"description":"Ramdev made controversial remarks about modern allopathic medicine during the COVID-19 pandemic, drawing condemnation from doctors and the Indian Medical Association.","details":null,"id":"3612","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Criticized Allopathy","year":"2021"},{"description":"Following criticism and legal notices over his comments on allopathic treatment, Ramdev issued a clarification and the dispute continued through public and legal channels.","details":null,"id":"3613","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Issued Clarification","year":"2021"},{"description":"Patanjali Foods, formerly Ruchi Soya Industries, returned to the stock market after a follow-on public offering and remained the group’s principal listed consumer-products company.","details":null,"id":"3614","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Listed Patanjali Foods","year":"2022"},{"description":"Ramdev stated that Patanjali planned public listings for additional group companies as part of a broader expansion strategy.","details":null,"id":"3615","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Outlined IPO Ambitions","year":"2022"},{"description":"An FIR was reported against Ramdev after allegations that remarks made during a public event hurt religious sentiments and promoted enmity.","details":null,"id":"3616","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Faced Religious Remarks Case","year":"2023"},{"description":"Patanjali came under intensified legal scrutiny over advertisements that allegedly disparaged modern medicine and made misleading claims about Ayurvedic products.","details":null,"id":"3617","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Faced Ad-Claims Litigation","year":"2023"},{"description":"The Supreme Court of India criticized Patanjali over misleading advertisements and required public apologies in proceedings concerning its advertising practices.","details":null,"id":"3618","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Received Supreme Court Rebuke","year":"2024"},{"description":"Ramdev and Acharya Balkrishna published a public apology in newspapers after the Supreme Court proceedings concerning Patanjali’s advertisements.","details":null,"id":"3619","side":"negative","timeline_id":"120","title":"Issued Public Apology","year":"2024"},{"description":"Ramdev continued leading the group’s public-facing promotion of Ayurveda, yoga, food, personal care, and consumer products amid ongoing regulatory scrutiny.","details":null,"id":"3620","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Continued Patanjali Expansion","year":"2024"},{"description":"He continued public yoga and Ayurveda advocacy and remained a prominent promoter of Patanjali-linked institutions and products.","details":null,"id":"3621","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Promoted Yoga And Ayurveda","year":"2025"},{"description":"By 2026, Baba Ramdev remained active as a yoga teacher, Ayurveda advocate, entrepreneur, and public campaigner associated with the Patanjali group.","details":null,"id":"3622","side":"positive","timeline_id":"120","title":"Remained Public Figure","year":"2026"},{"description":"Born as Rakesh Kumar in Lakhanpur village, Munger district, Bihar, to Shakuni Choudhary, a six-time MLA and MP, and Parvati Devi, also a legislator from Tarapur.","details":null,"id":"3623","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Born in Lakhanpur village","year":"16 Nov 1968"},{"description":"Began his political career with the Samata Party after completing basic education in Munger and higher education at Madurai Kamaraj University.","details":null,"id":"3624","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Entered active politics","year":"1990"},{"description":"Spent 89 days in jail during his early political years, a period later linked to the 1995 Tarapur case and recorded on the Bihar Legislative Council website.","details":null,"id":"3625","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Jailed for 89 days","year":"1995"},{"description":"Along with his parents and other Samata Party politicians, he joined Lalu Prasad Yadav's Rashtriya Janata Dal.","details":null,"id":"3626","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Joined Rashtriya Janata Dal","year":"1999"},{"description":"Sworn in as Minister of Horticulture, Weights and Measurement in the Rabri Devi ministry despite not being a member of either house of the legislature.","details":null,"id":"3627","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Became minister in Rabri government","year":"19 May 1999"},{"description":"Removed from the ministerial post following allegations that he was ineligible to hold office due to being underage at the time.","details":null,"id":"3628","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Removed over underage allegations","year":"16 Nov 1999"},{"description":"Won the Parbatta Assembly seat in Khagaria as an RJD candidate with 48,202 votes; his father was also elected to the assembly in the same election.","details":null,"id":"3629","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Elected MLA from Parbatta","year":"2000"},{"description":"BJP leader Sushil Kumar Modi alleged Choudhary was underage when filing his 2000 nomination and fought a legal battle against him.","details":null,"id":"3630","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Age eligibility legally challenged","year":"2003"},{"description":"His 2000 election was declared void by the court, and he lost the subsequent Parbatta by-election to Ramanand Prasad Singh of the JD(U).","details":null,"id":"3631","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Election voided, bypoll lost","year":"2004"},{"description":"Married Mamta Kumari, a lawyer by profession; the couple has a son, Pranay Priyam, and a daughter, Charu Priya.","details":null,"id":"3632","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Married Mamta Kumari","year":"2007"},{"description":"Won back the Parbatta seat as an RJD candidate, defeating Ramanand Prasad Singh by a narrow margin of 808 votes.","details":null,"id":"3633","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Re-elected from Parbatta","year":"24 Nov 2010"},{"description":"Made the chief whip of the opposition in the Bihar Legislative Assembly.","details":null,"id":"3634","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Appointed opposition chief whip","year":"2010"},{"description":"Entered the Bihar Legislative Council as a nominated member after leading a split in the RJD and joining the JD(U).","details":null,"id":"3635","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Became nominated MLC","year":"24 May 2014"},{"description":"Sworn in as Minister of Urban Development and Housing in the Jitan Ram Manjhi cabinet.","details":null,"id":"3636","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Urban Development Minister","year":"2 Jun 2014"},{"description":"His tenure as Urban Development and Housing Minister ended with the fall of the Manjhi government.","details":null,"id":"3637","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Ministerial tenure ended","year":"20 Feb 2015"},{"description":"Formally joined the Bharatiya Janata Party after growing disenchanted with the JD(U), beginning a rapid rise in the saffron party.","details":null,"id":"3638","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Joined the BJP","year":"2017"},{"description":"Appointed vice president of the BJP's Bihar state unit.","details":null,"id":"3639","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Made BJP state vice president","year":"2018"},{"description":"Elected unopposed to the Bihar Legislative Council on the BJP quota.","details":null,"id":"3640","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Elected MLC unopposed","year":"29 Jun 2020"},{"description":"Rose to prominence as a star campaigner for the BJP-led NDA in the 2020 Bihar Legislative Assembly election.","details":null,"id":"3641","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Star campaigner for NDA","year":"2020"},{"description":"Sworn in as Panchayati Raj Minister in the expanded Nitish Kumar cabinet, where he pushed staff recruitment and sanitation reforms.","details":null,"id":"3642","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Became Panchayati Raj Minister","year":"9 Feb 2021"},{"description":"Drew nationwide attention for a heated argument with Speaker Vijay Kumar Sinha over a departmental question, later apologizing for violating the decorum of the house.","details":null,"id":"3643","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Clashed with Assembly Speaker","year":"Mar 2021"},{"description":"Declared at the BJP's OBC convention in Khagaria that he and his party were not against a caste census, citing representation given to backward caste leaders.","details":null,"id":"3644","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Backed caste census","year":"2021"},{"description":"His tenure as Panchayati Raj Minister ended when Nitish Kumar's JD(U) broke with the BJP and left the NDA.","details":null,"id":"3645","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Lost cabinet berth","year":"9 Aug 2022"},{"description":"Selected as the Leader of the Opposition in the Bihar Legislative Council, succeeding Rabri Devi.","details":null,"id":"3646","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Became Leader of Opposition","year":"24 Aug 2022"},{"description":"Appointed president of the BJP's Bihar unit, replacing Sanjay Jaiswal, in a move seen as consolidating the Koeri-Kushwaha OBC vote base.","details":null,"id":"3647","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Appointed BJP Bihar president","year":"Mar 2023"},{"description":"Accused Chief Minister Nitish Kumar of promoting criminals and targeting saints after being stopped from meeting jailed former MLA Jawahar Prasad.","details":null,"id":"3648","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Attacked Nitish over criminals","year":"3 May 2023"},{"description":"Alleged JD(U) president Lalan Singh served liquor at a feast in Munger despite prohibition, prompting a censure resolution against him by the JD(U).","details":null,"id":"3649","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Liquor feast allegation row","year":"May 2023"},{"description":"Compared Rahul Gandhi's bearded appearance to Osama bin Laden, drawing widespread criticism.","details":null,"id":"3650","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Osama remark sparked controversy","year":"Jun 2023"},{"description":"Arrested along with other BJP leaders during a protest over job promises; police lathi-charged workers at Dak Bangla Square and one party worker died from injuries.","details":null,"id":"3651","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Arrested during Patna protest","year":"Jul 2023"},{"description":"Union minister Giriraj Singh projected Choudhary as the BJP's chief ministerial candidate for the 2025 Bihar election at a gathering in Begusarai.","details":null,"id":"3652","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Projected as BJP CM face","year":"2023"},{"description":"Sworn in as Deputy Chief Minister of Bihar with Finance and Sports portfolios after Nitish Kumar returned to the NDA.","details":null,"id":"3653","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Became Deputy Chief Minister","year":"28 Jan 2024"},{"description":"Presented a ₹2.79 lakh crore budget in the Bihar Assembly, among the biggest in the state's history, citing 10.64% growth and 2.5 crore people rising above poverty.","details":null,"id":"3654","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Presented record Bihar budget","year":"13 Feb 2024"},{"description":"Made convener of the Group of Ministers on GST rate rationalisation.","details":null,"id":"3655","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Convener of GST panel","year":"2024"},{"description":"Removed as BJP Bihar president after the 2024 Lok Sabha election, with the leadership concluding he failed to transfer Kushwaha votes; Dilip Kumar Jaiswal replaced him.","details":null,"id":"3656","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Removed as state BJP chief","year":"26 Jul 2024"},{"description":"Political strategist Prashant Kishor alleged Choudhary misrepresented his age before the Supreme Court in the 1995 Tarapur case using forged documents; the claims remain contested.","details":null,"id":"3657","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Age misrepresentation allegations","year":"2025"},{"description":"Won the Tarapur constituency with 122,480 votes (56.77%), defeating RJD's Arun Kumar Shah by 45,843 votes, as the BJP became the single largest party in Bihar.","details":null,"id":"3658","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Won Tarapur assembly seat","year":"14 Nov 2025"},{"description":"Elected leader of the BJP legislative party in Bihar following the assembly election victory.","details":null,"id":"3659","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Elected BJP legislature leader","year":"Nov 2025"},{"description":"Took charge of the Home Affairs Ministry in the tenth Nitish Kumar ministry, launching crackdowns on gangs, drugs, liquor and land mafias.","details":null,"id":"3660","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Took charge as Home Minister","year":"20 Nov 2025"},{"description":"Announced 100 fast-track courts for speedy justice and launched initiatives including the Abhay brigade, Pink Policing and a crime tracking network.","details":null,"id":"3661","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Announced fast-track courts","year":"7 Dec 2025"},{"description":"After Nitish Kumar announced his intention to resign and contest the Rajya Sabha elections, Choudhary was elected leader of the Bihar BJP legislative party.","details":null,"id":"3662","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Emerged as CM successor","year":"Mar 2026"},{"description":"Took oath as the 24th Chief Minister of Bihar, becoming the first BJP leader to hold the office in the state.","details":null,"id":"3663","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Sworn in as Chief Minister","year":"15 Apr 2026"},{"description":"Faced criticism after opposition leaders circulated videos alleging he struggled while reading the oath of office, with RJD supporters mocking the incident.","details":null,"id":"3664","side":"negative","timeline_id":"121","title":"Oath ceremony criticism","year":"Apr 2026"},{"description":"Directed private schools to declare fee structures and launched the satellite township program, Police Didi scheme and Sahyog Triveni helpline.","details":null,"id":"3665","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Launched governance schemes","year":"May 2026"},{"description":"Led the establishment of a technology centre at Deogaon village in Gaya district to train local youth for MSME sector jobs.","details":null,"id":"3666","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Set up Gaya technology centre","year":"May 2026"},{"description":"Launched a digital initiative allowing citizens above 75 years to register property from home, bypassing queues at registration centres.","details":null,"id":"3667","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Digital property registration launched","year":"Jul 2026"},{"description":"Approved the Gram Panchayat Taxes, Rates and Fees Rules 2026, enabling rural local bodies to collect holding taxes as part of a plan to raise state internal revenue to ₹1 lakh crore by 2028.","details":null,"id":"3668","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Approved panchayat tax rules","year":"Jul 2026"},{"description":"Launched subsidised heli tourism to sites like Valmikinagar and Kaimur, and signed a ₹6,000 crore MoU with the Mahashakti group for an integrated steel plant in Gaya.","details":null,"id":"3669","side":"positive","timeline_id":"121","title":"Heli tourism and steel MoU","year":"2026"},{"description":"Maya Boyd was born in Ann Arbor, Michigan, United States.","details":null,"id":"3683","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Born in Ann Arbor","year":"26 Nov 2002"},{"description":"Started performing through ballet before moving toward musical theatre.","details":null,"id":"3684","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Began ballet training","year":"Childhood"},{"description":"At age 13, she attended a summer intensive at Debbie Allen's dance academy in Los Angeles, having initially trained as a ballerina before shifting toward musical theatre.","details":null,"id":"3685","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Trained at Debbie Allen academy","year":"2016"},{"description":"Her early connection with Debbie Allen later developed into a professional relationship on Joe Turner's Come and Gone.","details":null,"id":"3686","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Met Debbie Allen","year":"2016"},{"description":"Enrolled at the University of Michigan School of Music, Theatre & Dance to study musical theatre.","details":null,"id":"3687","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Entered University of Michigan","year":"2020"},{"description":"Appeared in the University of Michigan production of Andrew Lippa's musical The Wild Party.","details":null,"id":"3688","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Performed in The Wild Party","year":"2021"},{"description":"Performed in the University of Michigan production of Hair during her musical-theatre training.","details":null,"id":"3689","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Performed in Hair","year":"2021"},{"description":"Appeared in the University of Michigan production of Rent as a student performer.","details":null,"id":"3690","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Performed in Rent","year":"2022"},{"description":"Performed in Sophisticated Ladies during her University of Michigan theatre studies.","details":null,"id":"3691","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Performed in Sophisticated Ladies","year":"2022"},{"description":"Was listed in the Broadway company of & Juliet before later taking over the title role.","details":null,"id":"3692","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Joined & Juliet company","year":"2022"},{"description":"Made her Broadway debut in Merrily We Roll Along at the Hudson Theatre while completing her senior year at the University of Michigan.","details":null,"id":"3693","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Made Broadway debut","year":"2023"},{"description":"Performed in the Broadway opening production of Maria Friedman's revival of Merrily We Roll Along.","details":null,"id":"3694","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Opened Merrily revival","year":"10 Oct 2023"},{"description":"Was credited as Mimi from Paramount in Merrily We Roll Along.","details":null,"id":"3695","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Played Mimi from Paramount","year":"2023"},{"description":"Was also credited as a Make-up Artist in Merrily We Roll Along.","details":null,"id":"3696","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Played Broadway makeup artist","year":"2023"},{"description":"Served as the understudy for Gussie Carnegie in Merrily We Roll Along.","details":null,"id":"3697","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Understudied Gussie Carnegie","year":"2023"},{"description":"Received a publicly listed acting credit in the screen project Deadbeat.","details":null,"id":"3698","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Appeared in Deadbeat","year":"2023"},{"description":"Concluded her Broadway engagement in Merrily We Roll Along after performing in the principal company and understudy team.","details":null,"id":"3699","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Completed Merrily run","year":"2024"},{"description":"Completed a Bachelor of Fine Arts in musical theatre at the University of Michigan.","details":null,"id":"3700","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Graduated from Michigan","year":"2024"},{"description":"The producers of & Juliet announced that Boyd would take over the title role in the Broadway production.","details":null,"id":"3701","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Announced as new Juliet","year":"16 Apr 2024"},{"description":"Began performing Juliet Capulet in & Juliet at the Stephen Sondheim Theatre.","details":null,"id":"3702","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Started playing Juliet","year":"14 May 2024"},{"description":"Led the Broadway pop musical & Juliet in the title role.","details":null,"id":"3703","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Headlined & Juliet","year":"2024"},{"description":"Completed her senior-year academic work while performing eight shows a week as Juliet.","details":null,"id":"3704","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Balanced college and Broadway","year":"2024"},{"description":"Attracted wider attention as the young replacement star of & Juliet after her Broadway debut in Merrily We Roll Along.","details":null,"id":"3705","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Gained Broadway recognition","year":"2024"},{"description":"Completed her documented Broadway engagement as Juliet Capulet in & Juliet.","details":null,"id":"3706","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Concluded & Juliet run","year":"2025"},{"description":"Moved from a contemporary pop musical toward a major American dramatic play with Joe Turner's Come and Gone.","details":null,"id":"3707","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Expanded dramatic repertoire","year":"2025"},{"description":"Was cast as Molly Cunningham in August Wilson's Joe Turner's Come and Gone at the Ethel Barrymore Theatre.","details":null,"id":"3708","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Joined Joe Turner revival","year":"2026"},{"description":"Began her Broadway engagement as Molly Cunningham in Joe Turner's Come and Gone, directed by Debbie Allen.","details":null,"id":"3709","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Started playing Molly Cunningham","year":"30 Mar 2026"},{"description":"Worked professionally with Debbie Allen after attending Allen's dance academy as a young performer.","details":null,"id":"3710","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Reunited with Debbie Allen","year":"2026"},{"description":"Appeared in an ensemble led by Taraji P. Henson and Cedric the Entertainer in Joe Turner's Come and Gone.","details":null,"id":"3711","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Performed with Taraji Henson","year":"2026"},{"description":"Portrayed Molly Cunningham in a revival of one of August Wilson's major American plays.","details":null,"id":"3712","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Played August Wilson role","year":"2026"},{"description":"Joe Turner's Come and Gone opened on Broadway with Boyd in the role of Molly Cunningham.","details":null,"id":"3713","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Opened Joe Turner revival","year":"25 Apr 2026"},{"description":"Concluded her scheduled Broadway engagement in Joe Turner's Come and Gone.","details":null,"id":"3714","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Completed Joe Turner run","year":"26 Jul 2026"},{"description":"Marvel announced that Boyd would play Ororo Munroe, also known as Storm, in the upcoming X-Men reboot directed by Jake Schreier.","details":null,"id":"3715","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Cast as Marvel's Storm","year":"14 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Her casting as Storm marked her first announced feature-film role and her transition from Broadway to a major film franchise.","details":null,"id":"3716","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Booked feature-film debut","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"Joined an ensemble including Sadie Sink as Jean Grey, Kit Connor as Cyclops, Samara Weaving as Emma Frost and Adam Driver as Mr. Sinister.","details":null,"id":"3717","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Joined X-Men ensemble","year":"2026"},{"description":"Moved from established Broadway roles into a globally recognized superhero property through her casting as Storm.","details":null,"id":"3718","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Began franchise transition","year":"2026"},{"description":"Began the next stage of her acting career by preparing to portray Storm in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.","details":null,"id":"3719","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Prepared for Storm role","year":"2026"},{"description":"The upcoming X-Men film featuring Boyd as Storm is scheduled for theatrical release on 5 May 2028.","details":null,"id":"3720","side":"positive","timeline_id":"123","title":"Scheduled X-Men release","year":"05 May 2028"},{"description":"Alireza Firouzja was born in Babol, Iran. He grew up in a family that supported his early interest in chess.","details":null,"id":"3753","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Born in Babol","year":"18 Jun 2003"},{"description":"He began playing chess at a very young age and quickly showed exceptional talent. His early progress marked him out as a future prodigy.","details":null,"id":"3754","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Started chess early","year":"2009"},{"description":"Firouzja began drawing attention in Iranian chess circles through youth competition results. His performances established him as one of the country’s most promising junior players.","details":null,"id":"3755","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Early national recognition","year":"2013"},{"description":"He earned the International Master title, confirming his status as one of the strongest young chess players in the world. This was an important step on his path to grandmaster level.","details":null,"id":"3756","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Became an International Master","year":"2016"},{"description":"Firouzja won the Iranian Chess Championship while still a teenager. The result increased his reputation as a top national talent.","details":null,"id":"3757","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Iranian Chess Championship","year":"2016"},{"description":"He started appearing in stronger international tournaments against experienced grandmasters. These appearances helped accelerate his development.","details":null,"id":"3758","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Played in elite events","year":"2016"},{"description":"His rapid rating growth and strong tournament results brought him wider international recognition. Chess fans and commentators began following his rise closely.","details":null,"id":"3759","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Entered the global spotlight","year":"2017"},{"description":"Firouzja won the Aeroflot Open, one of the most respected open chess tournaments. The victory was a major breakthrough in his career.","details":null,"id":"3760","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Aeroflot Open","year":"2018"},{"description":"He became a Grandmaster at a very young age. This title confirmed that he had reached the highest standard in over-the-board chess.","details":null,"id":"3761","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Earned Grandmaster title","year":"2018"},{"description":"Firouzja continued competing under the Iranian federation in major events. His results made him one of the most prominent young players from Asia.","details":null,"id":"3762","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Represented Iran internationally","year":"2018"},{"description":"He played in stronger European tournaments and invitationals. His performances against top grandmasters strengthened his reputation as a rising star.","details":null,"id":"3763","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"European and global exposure","year":"2019"},{"description":"Firouzja crossed new rating milestones as his form improved against world-class opposition. He became one of the youngest players to compete at the very top level.","details":null,"id":"3764","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Rating breakthrough","year":"2019"},{"description":"He made a strong mark in fast chess formats, where his tactical style suited the shorter time controls. These results helped build his international brand.","details":null,"id":"3765","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Played top rapid and blitz events","year":"2019"},{"description":"Firouzja and his family left Iran and later settled in France. This move became a major turning point in both his personal and chess life.","details":null,"id":"3766","side":"negative","timeline_id":"125","title":"Moved away from Iran","year":"2019"},{"description":"He began representing France in international chess. The switch gave him a new federation base for his career.","details":null,"id":"3767","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Became a French representative","year":"2020"},{"description":"During the rise of online chess, Firouzja posted strong performances in major internet events. His play against elite opposition kept him in the global spotlight.","details":null,"id":"3768","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Strong online chess results","year":"2020"},{"description":"He continued to perform well in rapid formats against the best players in the world. His versatility across formats became a defining strength.","details":null,"id":"3769","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Top-level rapid success","year":"2020"},{"description":"Firouzja became one of the youngest players ever to surpass a 2800 FIDE classical rating. This was a historic milestone in modern chess.","details":null,"id":"3770","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Crossed 2800 rating mark","year":"2021"},{"description":"Firouzja won Norway Chess, one of the strongest elite tournaments in classical chess. The result showed that he could defeat the very best in long-form play.","details":null,"id":"3771","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Norway Chess","year":"2021"},{"description":"He won the FIDE Grand Swiss, a major qualification tournament on the world chess calendar. That victory was one of the biggest achievements of his career.","details":null,"id":"3772","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won FIDE Grand Swiss","year":"2021"},{"description":"His victory at the FIDE Grand Swiss earned him a place in the Candidates cycle, the tournament that decides the challenger for the World Championship. This was one of the biggest achievements of his career.","details":null,"id":"3774","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Qualified for Candidates","year":"2021"},{"description":"Firouzja competed in the FIDE Candidates Tournament in Madrid against the strongest challengers in world chess. The event was a major test of his status at the top level.","details":null,"id":"3775","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Played Candidates Tournament","year":"2022"},{"description":"He experienced difficult results in some of the highest-pressure classical events. These setbacks showed the challenges of sustaining elite form against the world’s best.","details":null,"id":"3776","side":"negative","timeline_id":"125","title":"Faced pressure in elite competition","year":"2022"},{"description":"Firouzja won the Sinquefield Cup, one of the most prestigious classical tournaments in the Grand Chess Tour. The result confirmed his place among the strongest tournament players in the world.","details":null,"id":"3777","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Sinquefield Cup","year":"2022"},{"description":"He won the Saint Louis Rapid & Blitz, another key Grand Chess Tour event. The victory highlighted his strength across rapid and blitz formats.","details":null,"id":"3778","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Saint Louis Rapid & Blitz","year":"2022"},{"description":"Firouzja’s combined results in the Grand Chess Tour made him the overall 2022 Grand Chess Tour Champion. This was a major season-long achievement.","details":null,"id":"3779","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Grand Chess Tour","year":"2022"},{"description":"As one of the most recognizable young players in chess, he attracted commercial attention and brand visibility. His name became associated with the modern, media-friendly side of elite chess.","details":null,"id":"3781","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Built chess sponsorship profile","year":"2023"},{"description":"Firouzja won the Superbet Chess Classic Romania, a major event on the Grand Chess Tour. The victory added another important title to his elite tournament record.","details":null,"id":"3782","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Superbet Chess Classic Romania","year":"2024"},{"description":"He won the Sinquefield Cup again, confirming that his earlier success was not a one-off result. The tournament win reinforced his standing in classical chess.","details":null,"id":"3783","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Sinquefield Cup","year":"2024"},{"description":"Firouzja won the Saint Louis Rapid & Blitz once more, showing consistency in faster time controls. The result helped him remain one of the top all-format players in the world.","details":null,"id":"3784","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Saint Louis Rapid & Blitz","year":"2024"},{"description":"His strong Grand Chess Tour results in 2024 made him the overall champion of the series again. This repeated success placed him among the most accomplished players on the circuit.","details":null,"id":"3785","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Won Grand Chess Tour again","year":"2024"},{"description":"Firouzja scored another high finish at the FIDE Grand Swiss, keeping his profile strong in one of chess’s toughest qualification events. The result showed continuing consistency at elite level.","details":null,"id":"3787","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Strong Grand Swiss finish","year":"2025"},{"description":"Firouzja reached the late stages of the chess competition at the Esports World Cup. His run kept him in the spotlight as one of the leading modern chess stars.","details":null,"id":"3788","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Strong Esports World Cup run","year":"2026"},{"description":"He was involved in a high-profile and tense match against Hikaru Nakamura at the Esports World Cup. The moment drew attention because of the on-stage drama and emotional reaction.","details":null,"id":"3789","side":"positive","timeline_id":"125","title":"Tense third-place playoff","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"Vishal Garg was born in India; publicly available sources commonly place his birth in 1977 or 1978.","details":null,"id":"3791","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Born in India","year":"1977"},{"description":"Moved with his family from India to the United States at approximately eight years of age.","details":null,"id":"3792","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Moved to the United States","year":"1985"},{"description":"His family settled in Forest Hills, Queens, New York.","details":null,"id":"3793","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Settled in Queens","year":"1985"},{"description":"Began attending Stuyvesant High School in Manhattan.","details":null,"id":"3794","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Entered Stuyvesant High School","year":"1991"},{"description":"While in high school, worked as an entry clerk and runner for investment bank Salomon Brothers.","details":null,"id":"3795","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Started financial-services work","year":"1991"},{"description":"Graduated from Stuyvesant High School in Manhattan.","details":null,"id":"3796","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Graduated Stuyvesant High","year":"1995"},{"description":"Began undergraduate studies at New York University's Stern School of Business.","details":null,"id":"3797","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Entered NYU Stern","year":"1995"},{"description":"Completed bachelor's degrees in finance and international business from NYU Stern.","details":null,"id":"3798","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Earned two business degrees","year":"1998"},{"description":"Started work as an analyst in Morgan Stanley's mergers and acquisitions department.","details":null,"id":"3799","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Joined Morgan Stanley","year":"1998"},{"description":"Left Morgan Stanley around his 21st birthday and founded One Zero Capital, an early-stage investment firm.","details":null,"id":"3800","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Founded One Zero Capital","year":"1998"},{"description":"Through One Zero Capital, invested in technology companies in India and Latin America.","details":null,"id":"3801","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Focused on emerging markets","year":"1998"},{"description":"Co-founded MyRichUncle, an online student-lending company, with approximately $30,000 in initial capital.","details":null,"id":"3802","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Co-founded MyRichUncle","year":"1999"},{"description":"MyRichUncle developed into a data-driven private student lender serving borrowers in the United States.","details":null,"id":"3803","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Expanded student lending","year":"2000"},{"description":"Under Garg's leadership, MyRichUncle grew to employ approximately 300 people.","details":null,"id":"3804","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Built lending workforce","year":"2000"},{"description":"MyRichUncle became one of the largest private student lenders in the United States.","details":null,"id":"3805","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Reached major lender status","year":"2000"},{"description":"After building the student-lending company, Garg moved on to new financial-technology ventures.","details":null,"id":"3806","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Exited MyRichUncle period","year":"2010"},{"description":"Co-founded Future Finance with Brian Norton to provide student loans to university students in the United Kingdom.","details":null,"id":"3807","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Co-founded Future Finance","year":"2013"},{"description":"Future Finance expanded Garg's work in technology-enabled education lending beyond the United States.","details":null,"id":"3808","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Entered UK education finance","year":"2013"},{"description":"A difficult personal experience obtaining a mortgage helped motivate Garg to pursue a simpler digital mortgage process.","details":null,"id":"3809","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Experienced mortgage frustration","year":"2014"},{"description":"Founded Better.com as an online mortgage broker intended to streamline home financing.","details":null,"id":"3810","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Founded Better.com","year":"2014"},{"description":"Acquired Avex Funding of California to obtain mortgage licenses and an operating platform for online loan origination.","details":null,"id":"3811","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Acquired Avex Funding","year":"2014"},{"description":"Built Better's technology and lending operations around a branchless, digitally managed mortgage application process.","details":null,"id":"3812","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Developed digital mortgage platform","year":"2015"},{"description":"Better.com expanded its online mortgage business under Garg's leadership and attracted institutional investment.","details":null,"id":"3813","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Scaled Better operations","year":"2016"},{"description":"Better broadened its digital mortgage products and automated more of the home-financing process.","details":null,"id":"3815","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Expanded mortgage technology","year":"2018"},{"description":"The low-interest-rate housing environment helped drive increased activity across Better's digital mortgage platform. Increased hiring and operations during the mortgage-market expansion associated with the pandemic period.","details":null,"id":"3817","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Benefited from housing demand","year":"2020"},{"description":"Better increased hiring and operations during the mortgage-market expansion associated with the pandemic period.","details":null,"id":"3818","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Expanded company workforce","year":"2020"},{"description":"Garg became a prominent figure in financial technology as Better.com continued growing with backing from major investors including SoftBank.","details":null,"id":"3819","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Became high-profile fintech CEO","year":"2021"},{"description":"In a widely circulated Zoom meeting, Garg told approximately 900 Better.com employees that their employment was terminated immediately.","details":null,"id":"3820","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Announced mass Zoom layoffs","year":"05 Dec 2021"},{"description":"Garg apologized and acknowledged that he had mishandled the execution of the layoffs and failed to show appropriate respect and appreciation.","details":null,"id":"3822","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Apologized for layoff handling","year":"08 Dec 2021"},{"description":"Better.com's board announced that Garg would take time away from his chief executive duties while the company reviewed leadership and culture.","details":null,"id":"3823","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Took temporary leave","year":"10 Dec 2021"},{"description":"Returned to lead Better.com after his temporary leave and continued as the company's founder and chief executive.","details":null,"id":"3824","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Returned to CEO position","year":"2022"},{"description":"Better faced difficult market conditions as rising interest rates reduced mortgage refinancing and loan demand.","details":null,"id":"3825","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Managed mortgage downturn","year":"2022"},{"description":"Better Home & Finance completed a merger with Aurora Acquisition Corp., taking the mortgage-fintech company public through a SPAC transaction.","details":null,"id":"3827","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Completed public-listing merger","year":"2023"},{"description":"Better Home & Finance began trading on Nasdaq under the ticker BETR after completing its SPAC merger.","details":null,"id":"3828","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Better began public trading","year":"24 Aug 2023"},{"description":"The company's shares fell sharply on the first day of public trading, losing more than 90% of their value from the initial reference price.","details":null,"id":"3829","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Stock plunged after debut","year":"24 Aug 2023"},{"description":"The SPAC transaction provided Better with approximately $565 million in capital for continued operations and growth.","details":null,"id":"3830","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Unlocked public-market capital","year":"2023"},{"description":"Garg promoted artificial intelligence and automation as central parts of Better's effort to improve mortgage origination and reduce operating costs.","details":null,"id":"3831","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Pursued AI mortgage strategy","year":"2024"},{"description":"Continued overseeing restructuring and cost-control measures as Better attempted to stabilize its public business.","details":null,"id":"3833","side":"positive","timeline_id":"126","title":"Led restructuring efforts","year":"2025"},{"description":"Better disclosed cumulative GAAP net losses exceeding $1.5 billion since 2022, intensifying scrutiny of the company's performance under Garg.","details":null,"id":"3834","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Reported major cumulative losses","year":"2026"},{"description":"Stepped down as chief executive officer of Better Home & Finance, effective immediately, while remaining on the company's board.","details":null,"id":"3835","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Left Better CEO role","year":"03 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Better appointed board member Daniel Lewis as interim chief executive after Garg's departure from the CEO position.","details":null,"id":"3836","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Daniel Lewis became interim CEO","year":"03 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Better's board said it had terminated Garg as CEO after concerns about his judgment, temperament and credibility, while Garg sought changes to the board and challenged the company's leadership transition.","details":null,"id":"3837","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Faced board control dispute","year":"14 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Despite losing the CEO role, Garg continued to serve as a director of Better Home & Finance and remained involved in the dispute over the company's governance.","details":null,"id":"3838","side":"negative","timeline_id":"126","title":"Remained company director","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"Nithin Kamath was born in Shivamogga, Karnataka, to a Konkani family; his father U. R. Kamath worked at Canara Bank and his mother Revathi was a veena teacher.","details":null,"id":"3843","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Born in Shivamogga","year":"05 Oct 1979"},{"description":"The Kamath family relocated frequently across India due to his father's banking job, shaping his early schooling experience.","details":null,"id":"3844","side":"negative","timeline_id":"129","title":"Frequent family relocations","year":"1980"},{"description":"The Kamath family finally settled in Bangalore, where Nithin completed his secondary education.","details":null,"id":"3845","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Family settles in Bangalore","year":"1996"},{"description":"At age 17, Kamath began trading in the stock market, initially managing his father's trading account.","details":null,"id":"3846","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Begins stock trading","year":"1996"},{"description":"Kamath began working as a self-employed proprietary trader while still studying, a role he held until January 2004.","details":null,"id":"3847","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Starts proprietary trading","year":"Jan 1997"},{"description":"Kamath pursued a bachelor's degree in Electronics and Telecommunication Engineering at Bangalore Institute of Technology (BIT).","details":null,"id":"3848","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Enrolls at BIT","year":"1997"},{"description":"To supplement his trading income, Kamath worked as a Senior Tele-sales Associate at a call centre, trading during the day and working nights, until January 2004.","details":null,"id":"3849","side":"negative","timeline_id":"129","title":"Joins call centre job","year":"Jan 2001"},{"description":"Kamath completed his engineering degree from Bangalore Institute of Technology, balancing academics with active stock trading.","details":null,"id":"3850","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Graduates from BIT","year":"2001"},{"description":"Kamath began working as a sub-broker for Kamath Associates, a franchise of Reliance Money, offering portfolio advisory and proprietary trading services.","details":null,"id":"3851","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Becomes sub-broker","year":"Jan 2004"},{"description":"Nithin Kamath married Seema Patil in 2008; the couple later had a son named Kiaan.","details":null,"id":"3852","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Marries Seema Patil","year":"2008"},{"description":"Kamath concluded his tenure as a sub-broker for Kamath Associates after six years in the role.","details":null,"id":"3853","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Ends sub-broker role","year":"Jan 2010"},{"description":"Nithin Kamath co-founded Zerodha with his brother Nikhil Kamath, introducing a discount broking model with a flat fee of ₹20 per trade regardless of order size.","details":null,"id":"3854","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Co-founds Zerodha","year":"2010"},{"description":"Zerodha's flat-fee structure contrasted sharply with percentage-based fees charged by traditional Indian brokers, disrupting the industry.","details":null,"id":"3855","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Disrupts traditional brokerage","year":"2010"},{"description":"Zerodha launched its trading software Zerodha Trader, expanding digital access for retail investors.","details":null,"id":"3856","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Launches Zerodha Trader","year":"2013"},{"description":"Kamath received the Emerging Entrepreneur Award from the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII).","details":null,"id":"3857","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Wins CII entrepreneur award","year":"2014"},{"description":"Kamath founded Rainmatter, a fintech fund and incubator supporting startups in the financial technology space.","details":null,"id":"3858","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Founds Rainmatter","year":"2015"},{"description":"Zerodha introduced Kite, a streamlined online trading platform that simplified stock market access for retail users.","details":null,"id":"3859","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Launches Kite platform","year":"2015"},{"description":"The Economic Times listed Kamath among the Top 10 Businessmen in India for 2016.","details":null,"id":"3860","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Named top businessman","year":"2016"},{"description":"Zerodha was recognized as Startup of the Year (Bootstrap) by The Economic Times, highlighting its growth without external funding.","details":null,"id":"3861","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Wins Bootstrap Startup award","year":"2016"},{"description":"Zerodha launched Varsity, a free educational portal aimed at improving financial literacy among retail investors.","details":null,"id":"3862","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Launches Varsity education","year":"2016"},{"description":"Zerodha launched Coin, a platform enabling commission-free direct mutual fund investments for retail investors.","details":null,"id":"3863","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Introduces Zerodha Coin","year":"2017"},{"description":"Kamath was honored with the Forbes India Leadership Award in 2019 for his contributions to the fintech industry.","details":null,"id":"3864","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Receives Forbes India award","year":"2019"},{"description":"Kamath co-founded True Beacon, an investment management firm, together with his brother Nikhil Kamath.","details":null,"id":"3865","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Co-founds True Beacon","year":"2019"},{"description":"Zerodha reported a self-assessed valuation of approximately US$1 billion, achieved entirely through bootstrapping without venture capital.","details":null,"id":"3866","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Reaches billion-dollar valuation","year":"2020"},{"description":"Zerodha crossed 3 million active users, becoming India's largest stockbroker amid a pandemic-driven retail trading boom.","details":null,"id":"3867","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Becomes India's largest broker","year":"2020"},{"description":"Zerodha faced criticism after technical outages disrupted trading for users during periods of high market volatility.","details":null,"id":"3868","side":"negative","timeline_id":"129","title":"Faces platform outage criticism","year":"2021"},{"description":"Zerodha surpassed one crore (10 million) active clients, reinforcing its dominance as India's most trusted discount broker.","details":null,"id":"3869","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Crosses one crore clients","year":"2022"},{"description":"Kamath publicly commented on Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) regulations concerning derivatives trading and retail investor risk.","details":null,"id":"3870","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Advocates for regulatory reform","year":"2023"},{"description":"Kamath continued expanding Zerodha's ecosystem through Rainmatter and True Beacon, focusing on fintech growth and investor empowerment.","details":null,"id":"3871","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Expands fintech ecosystem","year":"2024"},{"description":"Kamath publicly cautioned retail investors about rising risks in futures and options trading amid a surge in speculative activity in India.","details":null,"id":"3872","side":"negative","timeline_id":"129","title":"Warns on trading risks","year":"2024"},{"description":"Kamath disclosed that he suffered a mild stroke, drawing attention to his health while he continued to lead Zerodha's operations.","details":null,"id":"3873","side":"negative","timeline_id":"129","title":"Suffers mild stroke","year":"Jan 2024"},{"description":"Kamath continued to be recognized among India's self-made billionaires, with Zerodha maintaining its position as the country's largest retail brokerage.","details":null,"id":"3875","side":"positive","timeline_id":"129","title":"Recognized as billionaire","year":"2026"},{"description":"Jeremiah Wells submitted Myktybek Orolbai with a ninja choke in the third round.","details":["Weight Class: Welterweight - Men","Gender: Men","Score: 14-4-1 vs 16-3-1","Technical Submission | R3 1:24","Match Date & Time: 15 Aug 2026 17:30 EDT","Fight #1"],"id":"3919","side":"positive","timeline_id":"135","title":"Match: 🏆 Jeremiah Wells (USA) - Myktybek Orolbai (KGZ)","year":"15 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Neil Magny stopped Ramiz Brahimaj with punches in the second round.","details":["Weight Class: Welterweight - Men","Gender: Men","Score: 32-15-0 vs 13-7-0","TKO | R2 3:20","Match Date & Time: 15 Aug 2026 18:00 EDT","Fight #2"],"id":"3920","side":"positive","timeline_id":"135","title":"Match: 🏆 Neil Magny (USA) - Ramiz Brahimaj (USA)","year":"15 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Lucas Fernando finished Rafael Tobias with a body-knee TKO in the third round.","details":["Weight Class: Light Heavyweight - Men","Gender: Men","Score: 14-3-0 vs 14-3-0","TKO | R3 1:10","Match Date & Time: 15 Aug 2026 18:30 EDT","Fight #3"],"id":"3921","side":"positive","timeline_id":"135","title":"Match: 🏆 Lucas Fernando (BRA) - Rafael Tobias (BRA)","year":"15 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Tresean Gore earned a unanimous decision over Vicente Luque.","details":["Weight Class: Middleweight - Men","Gender: Men","Score: 8-4-0 vs 24-13-1","Decision (Unanimous) | R3 5:00","Match Date & Time: 15 Aug 2026 19:00 EDT","Fight #4"],"id":"3922","side":"positive","timeline_id":"135