Khan, died of cancer when Shah Rukh Khan was a teenager.","details":null,"id":"3934","side":"negative","timeline_id":"136","title":"Lost his father","year":"1982"},{"description":"Joined Hans Raj College at the University of Delhi to study economics.","details":null,"id":"3935","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Entered Hans Raj College","year":"1985"},{"description":"Became associated with Delhi's Theatre Action Group, where he trained and performed under theatre director Barry John.","details":null,"id":"3936","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Joined theatre group","year":"1985"},{"description":"Left Hans Raj College before completing his degree in order to pursue acting and performance opportunities.","details":null,"id":"3937","side":"negative","timeline_id":"136","title":"Left college without graduating","year":"1988"},{"description":"Made his television acting debut in the series Dil Dariya.","details":null,"id":"3938","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Began television career","year":"1988"},{"description":"Played Abhimanyu Rai in the television series Fauji, gaining early recognition for his performance.","details":null,"id":"3939","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Acted in Fauji","year":"1989"},{"description":"Starred as Shekharan in the television series Circus.","details":null,"id":"3940","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Appeared in Circus","year":"1989"},{"description":"His mother, Lateef Fatima Khan, died after a prolonged illness.","details":null,"id":"3941","side":"negative","timeline_id":"136","title":"Lost his mother","year":"1990"},{"description":"Relocated from New Delhi to Mumbai to pursue a career in Hindi cinema.","details":null,"id":"3942","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Moved to Mumbai","year":"1991"},{"description":"Married Gauri Chhibber, later known as Gauri Khan, after a long courtship.","details":null,"id":"3943","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Married Gauri Chhibber","year":"25 Jun 1991"},{"description":"Made his Hindi-film debut as Raj in Deewana, which became a commercial success.","details":null,"id":"3944","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Made film debut","year":"1992"},{"description":"Won the Filmfare Award for Best Male Debut for Deewana.","details":null,"id":"3945","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won Filmfare debut award","year":"1992"},{"description":"Played Sunder Srivastava in the fantasy comedy Chamatkar.","details":null,"id":"3946","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Appeared in Chamatkar","year":"1992"},{"description":"Played Raju in the romantic comedy Raju Ban Gaya Gentleman.","details":null,"id":"3947","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Acted in Raju Ban Gaya Gentleman","year":"1992"},{"description":"Portrayed Ajay Sharma and Vicky Malhotra in Baazigar, taking on a morally complex lead role.","details":null,"id":"3948","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Played villain in Baazigar","year":"1993"},{"description":"Won the Filmfare Award for Best Actor for his performance in Baazigar.","details":null,"id":"3949","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won first Best Actor award","year":"1993"},{"description":"Played the obsessive Rahul Mehra in Darr, strengthening his reputation for intense and unconventional performances.","details":null,"id":"3950","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Darr","year":"1993"},{"description":"Played Sunil in Kabhi Haan Kabhi Naa, a role that earned him critical appreciation.","details":null,"id":"3951","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Acted in Kabhi Haan Kabhi Naa","year":"1994"},{"description":"Received the Filmfare Critics Award for Best Performance for Kabhi Haan Kabhi Naa.","details":null,"id":"3952","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won critics' acting award","year":"1994"},{"description":"Played Raj Malhotra opposite Kajol in Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge, one of the defining romantic films of Hindi cinema.","details":null,"id":"3953","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge","year":"1995"},{"description":"The success of Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge established him as one of Bollywood's leading romantic actors.","details":null,"id":"3954","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Became leading romantic star","year":"1995"},{"description":"Continued his rise with leading roles in films including English Babu Desi Mem and Army.","details":null,"id":"3955","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Married-screen image expanded","year":"1996"},{"description":"Played Rahul in Dil To Pagal Hai, a major romantic musical directed by Yash Chopra.","details":null,"id":"3956","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Dil To Pagal Hai","year":"1997"},{"description":"Won the Filmfare Award for Best Actor for Dil To Pagal Hai.","details":null,"id":"3957","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won Filmfare Best Actor","year":"1997"},{"description":"Played Rahul Khanna in Karan Johar's Kuch Kuch Hota Hai.","details":null,"id":"3958","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Kuch Kuch Hota Hai","year":"1998"},{"description":"Co-founded the production company Dreamz Unlimited with Juhi Chawla and director Aziz Mirza.","details":null,"id":"3959","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Founded Dreamz Unlimited","year":"1999"},{"description":"Made his debut as a film producer with Phir Bhi Dil Hai Hindustani through Dreamz Unlimited.","details":null,"id":"3960","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Produced Phir Bhi Dil Hai Hindustani","year":"2000"},{"description":"Played music teacher Raj Aryan Malhotra in Mohabbatein, which became a major commercial success.","details":null,"id":"3961","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Mohabbatein","year":"2000"},{"description":"Portrayed Emperor Ashoka in the historical film Aśoka.","details":null,"id":"3962","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Played Ashoka","year":"2001"},{"description":"Continued producing films through Dreamz Unlimited with the action drama One 2 Ka 4.","details":null,"id":"3963","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Produced One 2 Ka 4","year":"2001"},{"description":"Suffered recurring shoulder problems that later required surgery and affected his physical work schedule.","details":null,"id":"3964","side":"negative","timeline_id":"136","title":"Faced shoulder injury","year":"2001"},{"description":"Played the title role in Sanjay Leela Bhansali's Devdas, which premiered at the Cannes Film Festival.","details":null,"id":"3965","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Devdas","year":"2002"},{"description":"Devdas became one of the most internationally visible Hindi films of its period and increased Khan's global profile.","details":null,"id":"3966","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Received international recognition","year":"2002"},{"description":"Established Red Chillies Entertainment with Gauri Khan as a production and visual-effects company.","details":null,"id":"3967","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Co-founded Red Chillies","year":"2003"},{"description":"Played Major Ram Prasad Sharma in the action entertainer Main Hoon Na.","details":null,"id":"3968","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Main Hoon Na","year":"2004"},{"description":"Played Squadron Leader Veer Pratap Singh in Yash Chopra's Veer-Zaara.","details":null,"id":"3969","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Veer-Zaara","year":"2004"},{"description":"Won the Filmfare Award for Best Actor for Swades.","details":null,"id":"3970","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won Filmfare Best Actor","year":"2004"},{"description":"Red Chillies Entertainment produced Paheli, in which Khan also played the lead role.","details":null,"id":"3971","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Returned to production","year":"2005"},{"description":"Played Dev Saran in Karan Johar's relationship drama Kabhi Alvida Naa Kehna.","details":null,"id":"3972","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Kabhi Alvida Naa Kehna","year":"2006"},{"description":"Hosted the third season of the television quiz show Kaun Banega Crorepati.","details":null,"id":"3973","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Hosted Kaun Banega Crorepati","year":"2007"},{"description":"Played hockey coach Kabir Khan in Chak De India.","details":null,"id":"3974","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Chak De India","year":"2007"},{"description":"Won the Filmfare Award for Best Actor for Chak De India.","details":null,"id":"3975","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Won Filmfare Best Actor","year":"2007"},{"description":"Played Surinder Sahni and Raj in Rab Ne Bana Di Jodi.","details":null,"id":"3976","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Rab Ne Bana Di Jodi","year":"2008"},{"description":"Became a co-owner of the Kolkata Knight Riders franchise in the Indian Premier League.","details":null,"id":"3977","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Became Kolkata Knight Riders owner","year":"2008"},{"description":"Was awarded the Padma Shri by the Government of India for his contribution to Indian cinema.","details":null,"id":"3978","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Received Padma Shri","year":"2009"},{"description":"Played Rizwan Khan in My Name Is Khan, a performance that received major critical and international attention.","details":null,"id":"3979","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in My Name Is Khan","year":"2010"},{"description":"Headlined and produced the science-fiction superhero film Ra.One through Red Chillies Entertainment.","details":null,"id":"3980","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Ra.One","year":"2011"},{"description":"Played Samar Anand in Yash Chopra's final directorial film, Jab Tak Hai Jaan.","details":null,"id":"3981","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Jab Tak Hai Jaan","year":"2012"},{"description":"Produced and starred in Chennai Express, which became one of the highest-grossing Hindi films at the time.","details":null,"id":"3982","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Produced Chennai Express","year":"2013"},{"description":"Led the ensemble cast of Farah Khan's heist comedy Happy New Year.","details":null,"id":"3983","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Happy New Year","year":"2014"},{"description":"Reunited with Kajol for Rohit Shetty's romantic action film Dilwale.","details":null,"id":"3984","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Dilwale","year":"2015"},{"description":"Played both a superstar and his obsessive fan in Maneesh Sharma's Fan.","details":null,"id":"3985","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Fan","year":"2016"},{"description":"Played the title role in the crime drama Raees.","details":null,"id":"3986","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Raees","year":"2017"},{"description":"Played a tour guide in Imtiaz Ali's romantic drama Jab Harry Met Sejal.","details":null,"id":"3987","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Appeared in Jab Harry Met Sejal","year":"2017"},{"description":"Played Bauua Singh in the science-fiction romantic drama Zero.","details":null,"id":"3988","side":"positive","timeline_id":"136","title":"Starred in Zero","year":"2018"},{"description":"After Zero, took an extended break from leading acting roles following the film's disappointing commercial performance.","details":null,"id":"3989","side":"negative","timeline_id":"136","title":"Entered acting hiatus","year":"2018"},{"description":"Prepared several comeback projects after his acting hiatus, including Pathaan, Jawan and Dunki.","details":null,"id":"3990