":"Served as chief executive officer of the Maharashtra Khadi and Village Industries Board in Mumbai.","details":null,"id":"4088","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Led Khadi village industries","year":"2010"},{"description":"Completed a certificate course in Crisis, Emergency and Disaster Management at the National University of Singapore.","details":null,"id":"4089","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Completed Singapore certificate","year":"2011"},{"description":"Appointed district collector and district magistrate of Jalna.","details":null,"id":"4090","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Became Jalna collector","year":"Jun 2011"},{"description":"Appointed joint commissioner of Sales Tax in Mumbai. Worked on tax-evasion detection and revenue recovery during his sales-tax posting.","details":null,"id":"4092","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Joined Mumbai sales tax","year":"Sep 2012"},{"description":"Completed specialised training in tax analysis and revenue forecasting at Duke University.","details":null,"id":"4094","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Studied tax forecasting","year":"2014"},{"description":"Appointed district collector and district magistrate of Solapur. Led water-conservation and drought-mitigation efforts in Solapur through the Jalyukt Shivar programme.","details":null,"id":"4095","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Returned as Solapur collector","year":"Nov 2014"},{"description":"Received recognition commonly reported as the Maharashtra Waterman award for water-management efforts in Solapur.","details":null,"id":"4097","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Earned Waterman recognition","year":"2015"},{"description":"Appointed municipal commissioner of the Navi Mumbai Municipal Corporation.","details":null,"id":"4098","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Became Navi Mumbai commissioner","year":"May 2016"},{"description":"Initiated scrutiny of municipal revenue and property-tax processes in Navi Mumbai.","details":null,"id":"4099","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Started civic tax audit","year":"2016"},{"description":"Took action against encroachments, unauthorized constructions and alleged land-mafia activity in Navi Mumbai.","details":null,"id":"4100","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Targeted illegal construction","year":"2016"},{"description":"Introduced the Walk with Commissioner initiative to inspect civic conditions and interact directly with residents.","details":null,"id":"4101","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Launched Walk with Commissioner","year":"2016"},{"description":"Was abruptly transferred after less than a year as Navi Mumbai municipal commissioner, amid reported political opposition to his actions.","details":null,"id":"4102","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Transferred from Navi Mumbai","year":"24 Mar 2017"},{"description":"Appointed chairman and managing director of the Pune Mahanagar Parivahan Mahamandal Limited.","details":null,"id":"4103","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Led Pune transport corporation","year":"Apr 2017"},{"description":"Worked on bus-fleet optimisation, operational discipline and financial management at Pune's public transport undertaking.","details":null,"id":"4104","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Pursued PMPML reforms","year":"May 2017"},{"description":"Transferred to become municipal commissioner of the Nashik Municipal Corporation. Took action against unauthorized constructions and enforcement violations in Nashik.","details":null,"id":"4105","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Became Nashik commissioner","year":"Feb 2018"},{"description":"Removed from the Nashik municipal commissioner's post after approximately eight months amid reported opposition from political groups.","details":null,"id":"4107","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Transferred from Nashik","year":"Nov 2018"},{"description":"Posted as joint secretary in Maharashtra's Planning Department.","details":null,"id":"4108","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Joined planning department","year":"Nov 2018"},{"description":"Served as municipal commissioner of Nagpur during the COVID-19 pandemic and oversaw containment and public-health measures.","details":null,"id":"4109","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Led Nagpur COVID response","year":"2020"},{"description":"Was transferred from the Nagpur municipal commissioner's post after a short tenure amid disagreements over administrative decisions.","details":null,"id":"4110","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Transferred from Nagpur","year":"Aug 2020"},{"description":"Continued serving in senior Maharashtra government assignments after his Nagpur posting.","details":null,"id":"4111","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Handled administrative assignments","year":"2021"},{"description":"Served as commissioner of Health Services and managing director of the National Health Mission in Maharashtra.","details":null,"id":"4112","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Led health services","year":"2022"},{"description":"By this period, his career had become associated with frequent transfers across field, civic and secretariat assignments.","details":null,"id":"4115","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Reached repeated-transfer milestone","year":"2024"},{"description":"His name entered public discussion during political controversy surrounding a land transaction in Pune, although reports did not establish personal wrongdoing by him.","details":null,"id":"4116","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Faced land-deal controversy","year":"2025"},{"description":"Reports stated that he had faced approximately 23 transfers in 20 years of service, making his posting history unusually mobile.","details":null,"id":"4117","side":"negative","timeline_id":"140","title":"Recorded twenty-third transfer","year":"2025"},{"description":"Was transferred to responsibilities involving Revenue, Relief and Rehabilitation, and Disaster Management in Maharashtra.","details":null,"id":"4118","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Received disaster-management posting","year":"31 Mar 2026"},{"description":"Appointed commissioner of Maharashtra's Food and Drug Administration.","details":null,"id":"4119","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Became FDA commissioner","year":"May 2026"},{"description":"Directed inspections, raids and enforcement action against food-safety violations and establishments allegedly breaching prescribed standards.","details":null,"id":"4120","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Launched food-safety crackdown","year":"Jun 2026"},{"description":"Maharashtra's FDA issued notices to actors associated with advertisements for a pan-masala brand whose products were reported as banned in the state.","details":null,"id":"4121","side":"positive","timeline_id":"140","title":"Issued pan-masala notices","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"Gurmeet Ram Rahim Singh was born on 15 August 1967 at Sri Gurusar Modia village in Sri Ganganagar district, Rajasthan, into a Sikh family.","details":null,"id":"4123","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Born in Rajasthan village","year":"15 Aug 1967"},{"description":"At age 7, Singh was initiated into the Dera Sacha Sauda sect by then-leader Shah Satnam Singh, accompanying his father to the dera.","details":null,"id":"4124","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Initiated into Dera sect","year":"1974"},{"description":"As a young adult, Singh worked at various jobs including driving a tractor and assisted his father in volunteer work at the dera.","details":null,"id":"4125","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Various jobs before succession","year":"1970s-1980s"},{"description":"Shah Satnam Singh unexpectedly announced his retirement and appointed 23-year-old Gurmeet as his successor, naming him 'Huzoor Maharaj Gurmeet Ram Rahim'.","details":null,"id":"4126","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Named Dera Sacha Sauda chief","year":"23 Sep 1990"},{"description":"A woman wrote to state chief ministers, the Union Home Minister, CBI, NHRC and the High Court alleging rape by Ram Rahim, triggering a judicial inquiry.","details":null,"id":"4127","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Anonymous rape complaint filed","year":"2002"},{"description":"The Punjab and Haryana High Court ordered a CBI investigation into the rape allegations after an inquiry by a Sirsa district judge recommended a central probe.","details":null,"id":"4128","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"CBI probe ordered","year":"24 Sep 2002"},{"description":"Journalist Ram Chander Chhatrapati, who published the rape complaint letter, was murdered; Ram Rahim was later charged in connection with the killing.","details":null,"id":"4129","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Journalist murder allegation","year":"2002"},{"description":"Ram Rahim also faced charges over the murder of Dera manager Ranjit Singh in the same period, later acquitted by the High Court.","details":null,"id":"4130","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Dera manager murder charge","year":"2002"},{"description":"Singh began his foray into music and later films, positioning himself as a singer-songwriter and eventually actor-director under the Dera's production banner.","details":null,"id":"4131","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"First films and albums launched","year":"2007"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was accused of hurting Sikh religious sentiments by dressing in an outfit resembling Guru Gobind Singh, sparking protests.","details":null,"id":"4132","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sikh sentiment controversy erupts","year":"May 2007"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was attacked by a mob amid the Sikh sentiment controversy but escaped unhurt.","details":null,"id":"4133","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Attacked by protesting mob","year":"16 Jul 2007"},{"description":"An explosive attack on Ram Rahim's cavalcade injured 11 people; a Khalistan Liberation Force member was later arrested for the plot.","details":null,"id":"4134","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Cavalcade bomb attack","year":"2 Feb 2008"},{"description":"Sikh protestors clashed with Dera followers during Ram Rahim's visit to a Mumbai mall, resulting in the death of one protestor.","details":null,"id":"4135","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Mumbai mall altercation","year":"20 Jun 2008"},{"description":"Ram Rahim initiated a campaign to rescue women from forced prostitution, motivating around 1,500 male followers to marry rescued women.","details":null,"id":"4136","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Anti-prostitution rehabilitation drive","year":"2009"},{"description":"A criminal case against Ram Rahim for hurting Sikh sentiments was dismissed by the Sirsa court.","details":null,"id":"4137","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sikh sentiment case dismissed","year":"2009"},{"description":"Ram Rahim began mega cleanliness and sanitation drives in New Delhi, later expanding to dozens of campaigns across India.","details":null,"id":"4138","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Launched cleanliness campaigns","year":"21 Sep 2011"},{"description":"Dera's backing of the Congress party in the 2012 Punjab elections was seen as politically damaging, coinciding with poor Congress performance.","details":null,"id":"4139","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Congress support falters","year":"2012"},{"description":"Ram Rahim released his debut album 'Thank You For That' under Universal, followed by several more albums that year.","details":null,"id":"4140","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Commercial music debut","year":"2012"},{"description":"A second criminal case over hurt Sikh religious sentiments was dismissed by a Bathinda court.","details":null,"id":"4141","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sikh case dismissed again","year":"2014"},{"description":"Ram Rahim told the special CBI court he had been impotent since 1990 in defense against the rape charges; the court rejected the claim.","details":null,"id":"4142","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Claimed impotence in court","year":"2014"},{"description":"His album 'Highway Love Charger' reportedly sold 3 million copies within three days and became a viral YouTube hit.","details":null,"id":"4143","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Highway Love Charger album hit","year":"2014"},{"description":"Ahead of the 2014 Haryana elections, PM Narendra Modi courted Ram Rahim's support, and the Dera backed the BJP.","details":null,"id":"4144","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Supported BJP in Haryana polls","year":"2014"},{"description":"Ram Rahim made his film debut as director, writer and lead actor in 'MSG: The Messenger', earning four IFPI Platinum Plaques for its music.","details":null,"id":"4145","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Film directing debut MSG","year":"2015"},{"description":"He released 'MSG-2 The Messenger', continuing his self-focused film franchise, though critics panned the productions.","details":null,"id":"4146","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sequel MSG-2 released","year":"2015"},{"description":"The Indian Express ranked Ram Rahim 96th on its list of the 100 most powerful Indians of 2015.","details":null,"id":"4147","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Named among powerful Indians","year":"2015"},{"description":"The Akal Takht initially pardoned Ram Rahim for the 2007 Sikh sentiment controversy amid the film releases.","details":null,"id":"4148","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Akal Takht pardon granted","year":"27 Sep 2015"},{"description":"Following widespread Sikh protest, the Akal Takht revoked its earlier pardon of Ram Rahim.","details":null,"id":"4149","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Akal Takht revokes pardon","year":"16 Oct 2015"},{"description":"Ram Rahim released his third film, unveiling a song at a live concert before an audience of 3.6 million fans.","details":null,"id":"4150","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"MSG: Warrior Lion Heart released","year":"2016"},{"description":"A ₹5 million government grant to the Dera for sports promotion, announced in Ram Rahim's presence, triggered public controversy.","details":null,"id":"4151","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Haryana sports grant controversy","year":"2016"},{"description":"Ram Rahim's portrayal of the god Vishnu prompted a complaint from the Vishwa Hindu Parishad in January 2016.","details":null,"id":"4152","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Dressed as Hindu god Vishnu","year":"2016"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was nominated for the Dronacharya Award by the Yoga Federation of India for training champion yogis.","details":null,"id":"4153","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Dronacharya Award nomination","year":"2017"},{"description":"A special CBI court in Panchkula found Ram Rahim guilty of two counts of rape of a former sadhvi, and he was taken into custody amid violent protests that killed dozens.","details":null,"id":"4154","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Convicted of rape","year":"25 Aug 2017"},{"description":"The CBI court sentenced Ram Rahim to 20 years in prison, 10 years for each rape conviction, to run consecutively.","details":null,"id":"4155","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sentenced to 20 years","year":"28 Aug 2017"},{"description":"The IFTDA and CINTAA banned Ram Rahim from future work in Indian film and television for 'criminality and moral turpitude'.","details":null,"id":"4156","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Banned from film industry","year":"2 Sep 2017"},{"description":"Ram Rahim challenged his rape conviction before the Punjab and Haryana High Court.","details":null,"id":"4157","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Appealed rape conviction","year":"9 Oct 2017"},{"description":"The United Nations Water Body invited the convicted Ram Rahim to a World Toilet Day event, later deleting the tweets without explanation.","details":null,"id":"4158","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"UN invitation controversy","year":"4 Oct 2017"},{"description":"Ram Rahim and three others were convicted of murdering journalist Ram Chander Chhatrapati and sentenced to life imprisonment.","details":null,"id":"4159","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Convicted of journalist's murder","year":"Jan 2019"},{"description":"A Panchkula CBI court granted Ram Rahim bail in the case involving forced castration of 400 followers.","details":null,"id":"4160","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Granted bail in castration case","year":"5 Oct 2018"},{"description":"A special CBI court found Ram Rahim and four others guilty of the 2002 murder of former Dera manager Ranjit Singh.","details":null,"id":"4161","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Convicted in manager's murder","year":"Oct 2021"},{"description":"Punjab Police found evidence linking Ram Rahim to over 107 cases of alleged sacrilege of the Guru Granth Sahib.","details":null,"id":"4162","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Sacrilege cases evidence found","year":"8 Nov 2021"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was granted one day of secretly arranged parole to visit his ailing mother in a Gurgaon hospital.","details":null,"id":"4163","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"First one-day parole","year":"24 Oct 2020"},{"description":"He received a 12-hour release, from sunrise to sunset, to again visit his unwell mother under police protection.","details":null,"id":"4164","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"12-hour parole granted","year":"21 May 2021"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was granted a 21-day furlough to meet family, provided with Z-plus security.","details":null,"id":"4165","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"21-day furlough approved","year":"Feb 2022"},{"description":"He was granted a 30-day parole, staying at the Dera's Barnawa Ashram in Baghpat, Uttar Pradesh, despite SGPC objections.","details":null,"id":"4166","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"30-day parole at Barnawa","year":"Jun 2022"},{"description":"During a 40-day parole, Ram Rahim released three music videos on his YouTube channel, drawing criticism from the Delhi Commission for Women.","details":null,"id":"4167","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"40-day parole and music releases","year":"14 Oct 2022"},{"description":"Ram Rahim received another 40-day parole and was filmed cutting a cake with a sword, an act later flagged as illegal under the Arms Act.","details":null,"id":"4168","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"40-day parole, sword incident","year":"21 Jan 2023"},{"description":"While out on parole, Ram Rahim's volunteers organised two mega cleanliness campaigns across Haryana and Rajasthan.","details":null,"id":"4169","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Cleanliness drives resumed","year":"Early 2023"},{"description":"Ram Rahim received another 30-day parole period during 2023.","details":null,"id":"4170","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"30-day parole granted","year":"20 Jul 2023"},{"description":"He was granted a further 21-day parole later in 2023.","details":null,"id":"4171","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"21-day parole granted","year":"20 Nov 2023"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was granted a 50-day parole to stay at his Barnawa Ashram in Baghpat, Uttar Pradesh.","details":null,"id":"4172","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"50-day parole approved","year":"19 Jan 2024"},{"description":"The Punjab and Haryana High Court ordered the Haryana government not to grant Ram Rahim parole without court approval.","details":null,"id":"4173","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"High Court restricts paroles","year":"26 Feb 2024"},{"description":"The Punjab and Haryana High Court acquitted Ram Rahim and four others in the 2002 murder of Dera manager Ranjit Singh, overturning the 2021 conviction.","details":null,"id":"4174","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Acquitted in manager murder","year":"28 May 2024"},{"description":"The SGPC strongly criticised repeated parole grants to Ram Rahim, calling it a political vote-bank strategy ahead of Haryana elections.","details":null,"id":"4175","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"SGPC objects to paroles","year":"13 Aug 2024"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was granted 20 days' parole ahead of the Haryana assembly elections, with strict conditions barring political activity.","details":null,"id":"4176","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"20-day pre-election parole","year":"2 Oct 2024"},{"description":"Ahead of Delhi Assembly elections, Ram Rahim received 30 days' parole, spending time at both Sirsa headquarters and Barnawa Ashram.","details":null,"id":"4177","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"30-day parole before Delhi polls","year":"28 Jan 2025"},{"description":"The Supreme Court of India dismissed a PIL challenging Ram Rahim's repeated temporary releases, citing maintainability concerns.","details":null,"id":"4178","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"Supreme Court dismisses PIL","year":"28 Feb 2025"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was granted a 21-day furlough to stay at the Dera headquarters in Sirsa, Haryana.","details":null,"id":"4179","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"21-day furlough at Sirsa","year":"9 Apr 2025"},{"description":"During a 40-day parole coinciding with his birthday, Ram Rahim organised a tree plantation drive and flood relief initiatives for Punjab.","details":null,"id":"4180","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"40-day parole and flood relief","year":"5 Aug 2025"},{"description":"Ram Rahim received his 15th parole since 2017, for 40 days, to attend the birth anniversary of former Dera chief Shah Satnam Singh virtually.","details":null,"id":"4181","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"15th parole, 40 days","year":"4 Jan 2026"},{"description":"The Punjab and Haryana High Court acquitted Ram Rahim in the 2002 murder of journalist Ram Chander Chhatrapati, reversing his 2019 life sentence conviction.","details":null,"id":"4182","side":"positive","timeline_id":"141","title":"Acquitted in journalist murder","year":"7 Mar 2026"},{"description":"Ram Rahim was released on his 16th parole since 2017, a 30-day period spent at the Dera headquarters in Sirsa, exhausting his annual parole quota.","details":null,"id":"4183","side":"negative","timeline_id":"141","title":"16th parole granted","year":"25 May 2026"},{"description":"Gamage Sonal Dinusha was born in Colombo, Sri Lanka.","details":null,"id":"4184","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Born in Colombo","year":"04 Dec 2000"},{"description":"Dinusha grew up in Colombo and developed as a left-handed batter and slow left-arm orthodox bowler.","details":null,"id":"4185","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Early life in Colombo","year":"2000s"},{"description":"He was educated at Mahanama College in Colombo, a school with a strong cricket tradition.","details":null,"id":"4186","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Attended Mahanama College","year":"2010s"},{"description":"During his school-cricket years, Dinusha developed his skills as a batting all-rounder who could also bowl left-arm spin.","details":null,"id":"4187","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Developed as an all-rounder","year":"2010s"},{"description":"Dinusha was selected for the Sri Lanka Under-19 side to play against the visiting India Under-19 team.","details":null,"id":"4188","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Selected for Sri Lanka Under-19s","year":"2018"},{"description":"He made his first-class debut for Colombo Cricket Club during the 2018-19 domestic season.","details":null,"id":"4189","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"First-class debut","year":"2018"},{"description":"In his first-class debut match, Dinusha scored 59 batting at number three in the second innings.","details":null,"id":"4190","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Impressed in debut match","year":"2018"},{"description":"He began gaining experience in youth international cricket through Sri Lanka Under-19 fixtures.","details":null,"id":"4191","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Under-19 international exposure","year":"2018"},{"description":"Dinusha represented Sri Lanka at the 2020 ICC Under-19 Cricket World Cup.","details":null,"id":"4194","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"ICC Under-19 World Cup","year":"2020"},{"description":"Following the Under-19 World Cup, he continued to build his record in Sri Lankan domestic cricket.","details":null,"id":"4195","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Built domestic experience","year":"2020"},{"description":"He began appearing in domestic Twenty20 cricket for Colombo Cricket Club during the 2020-21 season.","details":null,"id":"4196","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"T20 domestic cricket","year":"2020"},{"description":"Dinusha continued establishing himself as a productive all-rounder in Sri Lanka's domestic first-class competitions.","details":null,"id":"4197","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Progressed in first-class cricket","year":"2021"},{"description":"His slow left-arm orthodox bowling became an additional asset alongside his left-handed batting.","details":null,"id":"4198","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Developed spin-bowling role","year":"2021"},{"description":"Dinusha joined Fulwood and Broughton as its overseas professional in the Northern Premier Cricket League in England.","details":null,"id":"4199","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Played English club cricket","year":"2022"},{"description":"He finished as the Northern Premier Cricket League's leading run-scorer with 937 runs in 21 matches for Fulwood and Broughton.","details":null,"id":"4200","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Leading run-scorer in league","year":"2022"},{"description":"In the same English league season, Dinusha took 60 wickets and finished as the competition's second-highest wicket-taker.","details":null,"id":"4201","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Second-highest wicket-taker","year":"2022"},{"description":"After his English club stint, he returned to continue his professional development in Sri Lanka's domestic competitions.","details":null,"id":"4202","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Returned to Sri Lankan domestic cricket","year":"2022"},{"description":"Dinusha played franchise cricket for Galle Titans in the Lanka Premier League.","details":null,"id":"4203","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Represented Galle Titans","year":"2023"},{"description":"He represented Sri Lanka Emerging, gaining experience in the national development pathway.","details":null,"id":"4204","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Sri Lanka Emerging representation","year":"2023"},{"description":"Dinusha represented Sri Lanka A, moving closer to senior international selection.","details":null,"id":"4205","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Sri Lanka A selection","year":"2023"},{"description":"He represented Dambulla Sixers in franchise T20 cricket.","details":null,"id":"4206","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Joined Dambulla Sixers","year":"2024"},{"description":"Dinusha earned selection in Sri Lanka's Test squad after his domestic and representative-team performances.","details":null,"id":"4209","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Named in Sri Lanka Test squad","year":"2025"},{"description":"Dinusha made his Test debut for Sri Lanka against Bangladesh at Sinhalese Sports Club in Colombo.On his Test debut he took wickets with his left-arm spin and Dinusha scored 11 runs in his first Test innings","details":null,"id":"4210","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Test debut","year":"25 Jun 2025"},{"description":"His debut established him as a Test-capped Sri Lankan international cricketer.","details":null,"id":"4213","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Test-capped Sri Lankan all-rounder","year":"2025"},{"description":"Dinusha scored his 11th first-class century while representing Sri Lanka A against New Zealand A.","details":null,"id":"4215","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Sri Lanka A against New Zealand A","year":"2026"},{"description":"He reached his 11th first-class hundred in the Sri Lanka A match against New Zealand A.","details":null,"id":"4216","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Eleventh first-class century","year":"17 Apr 2026"},{"description":"Dinusha played for Sri Lanka in a Test match against India at Galle.","details":null,"id":"4218","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Test against India","year":"15 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Against India at Galle, Dinusha scored his maiden Test century, making 100 from 168 balls in Sri Lanka's first innings.","details":null,"id":"4219","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Maiden Test century","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"His maiden Test hundred helped Sri Lanka recover from a difficult position and reach 284 in the first innings against India.","details":null,"id":"4220","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Rescued Sri Lanka innings","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"By 2026, Dinusha had built a first-class record featuring more than 3,500 runs, more than 130 wickets and multiple centuries.","details":null,"id":"4221","side":"positive","timeline_id":"142","title":"Growing first-class record","year":"2026"},{"description":"Samay Raina was born in Jammu city in the erstwhile Indian state of Jammu and Kashmir into a conservative Kashmiri Pandit family with roots in the Salia area of Seer Hamdan, Anantnag.","details":null,"id":"4222","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Born in Jammu","year":"26 Oct 1997"},{"description":"Raina completed his schooling at Hyderabad Public School, Begumpet, after his family moved from Jammu.","details":null,"id":"4223","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Schooling in Hyderabad","year":"2010s"},{"description":"Raina enrolled at Pune Vidhyarthi Griha's College of Engineering and Technology (PVG's COET) in Pune, Maharashtra, to study Printing Engineering.","details":null,"id":"4224","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Enrolled at PVG's COET","year":"2015"},{"description":"Raina completed his B.E. in Printing Technology Engineering from PVG's College of Engineering and Technology, Pune, though he later described the course as not useful for his career.","details":null,"id":"4225","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Completed Engineering Degree","year":"2019"},{"description":"While in Pune, Raina began performing at open mic comedy events, finding his calling in stand-up comedy over his engineering studies.","details":null,"id":"4226","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Started Open Mic Comedy","year":"2017"},{"description":"Raina competed in Amazon Prime Video's Comicstaan Season 2, which premiered on 12 July 2019, mentored by judge Kanan Gill.","details":null,"id":"4227","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Comicstaan Season 2 Premiere","year":"12 Jul 2019"},{"description":"Raina was announced as joint winner of Comicstaan Season 2 alongside Aakash Gupta at the grand finale held at the Grand Opera House in Mumbai, receiving the trophy and a cash prize of Rs 10 lakh.","details":null,"id":"4228","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Won Comicstaan Season 2","year":"16 Aug 2019"},{"description":"During the COVID-19 lockdown, with live comedy shows cancelled, Raina began streaming chess on his YouTube channel, blending comedy with chess entertainment.","details":null,"id":"4229","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Started YouTube Streaming","year":"2020"},{"description":"Raina began the 'Improving Chess with Comedians' series with IM Sagar Shah of ChessBase India, training alongside comedians Biswa Kalyan Rath, Vaibhav Sethia, and Anirban Dasgupta.","details":null,"id":"4230","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Improving Chess Series Began","year":"19 May 2020"},{"description":"The 'Improving Chess with Comedians' series completed 100 episodes over 124 days on ChessBase India, becoming one of the most loved chess series of the lockdown.","details":null,"id":"4231","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"100 Chess Episodes Completed","year":"23 Sep 2020"},{"description":"Raina's streams with grandmasters and comedians sparked a chess boom in India, drawing massive audiences and collaborations with players like Vidit Gujrathi and streamers like the Botez sisters.","details":null,"id":"4232","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Popularized Chess Streaming India","year":"2020"},{"description":"Raina co-hosted the Checkmate COVID simultaneous exhibition on Chess.com featuring Viswanathan Anand, Koneru Humpy, Harika Dronavalli, Nihal Sarin, and Praggnanandhaa, raising funds for Red Cross India and AICF's COVID relief initiative.","details":null,"id":"4233","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Checkmate COVID Charity Event","year":"13 May 2021"},{"description":"Raina organized multiple charity chess streams during the second COVID-19 wave in India, raising significant funds for relief work through his YouTube channel.","details":null,"id":"4234","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Chess Charity Fundraisers","year":"2021"},{"description":"Raina launched India's Got Latent, a Hindi comedy talent show on his YouTube channel, featuring contestants performing with celebrity guest judges; he also launched a companion app on iOS and Android.","details":null,"id":"4236","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Launched India's Got Latent","year":"14 Jun 2024"},{"description":"India's Got Latent became a record-breaking digital hit, with clips dominating Indian social media and members-only episodes driving massive paid subscriptions on YouTube.","details":null,"id":"4237","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"India's Got Latent Went Viral","year":"2024"},{"description":"Propelled by India's Got Latent's popularity, Raina's YouTube channel grew to become one of India's most-subscribed independent comedy channels.","details":null,"id":"4238","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"YouTube Subscriber Surge","year":"2024"},{"description":"A clip from a members-only episode went viral in which guest judge Ranveer Allahbadia asked a contestant an explicit and inappropriate question, triggering nationwide outrage and criticism of the show's content.","details":null,"id":"4239","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"India's Got Latent Controversy Erupted","year":"10 Feb 2025"},{"description":"Multiple FIRs were filed against Raina, Allahbadia, and fellow panelists Ashish Chanchlani and Apoorva Makhija across several states, with police complaints lodged in Mumbai and Guwahati; the National Commission for Women issued notices and the Maharashtra Cyber Cell opened an inquiry.","details":null,"id":"4240","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Multiple FIRs Filed","year":"Feb 2025"},{"description":"Raina removed all episodes of India's Got Latent from his YouTube channel, stating he would fully cooperate with investigating agencies; the deletion reportedly cost hundreds of millions of views.","details":null,"id":"4241","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Removed All India's Got Latent Episodes","year":"12 Feb 2025"},{"description":"The controversy effectively ended India's Got Latent and caused Raina's professional calendar to collapse overnight, with shows cancelled amid the backlash.","details":null,"id":"4242","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Show Shut Down, Bookings Collapsed","year":"Feb 2025"},{"description":"During the second day of the controversy, Raina recorded nine separate apology videos but published none, later revealing the backlash caused severe mental health struggles.","details":null,"id":"4243","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Recorded Nine Unposted Apologies","year":"Feb 2025"},{"description":"The Supreme Court protected co-accused Ranveer Allahbadia from arrest in the multiple FIRs and directed him to deposit his passport with the Thane Cyber Police, as the cases against the show's panel proceeded.","details":null,"id":"4244","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Supreme Court Granted Protection","year":"18 Feb 2025"},{"description":"The Supreme Court said it would examine a fresh plea alleging Raina ridiculed persons with disabilities, including a person with visual disability and those suffering from Spinal Muscular Atrophy, on his show.","details":null,"id":"4245","side":"negative","timeline_id":"143","title":"Fresh Plea Over Disability Remarks","year":"21 Apr 2025"},{"description":"Raina announced his return to the stage with the 'Still Alive and Unfiltered' international tour spanning Europe, the UK, Australia, and New Zealand, from Cologne on 5 June to Sydney on 20 July.","details":null,"id":"4246","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Announced International Comeback Tour","year":"13 May 2025"},{"description":"Raina announced his first India tour since the controversy, 'Samay Raina Is Still Alive and Unfiltered', presented by BookMyShow, selling 40,000 tickets within an hour of going live.","details":null,"id":"4247","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Announced India Comeback Tour","year":"31 Jul 2025"},{"description":"Raina opened his multi-city India tour in Bengaluru, with shows running through Hyderabad, Mumbai, Kolkata, Chennai, and Pune, concluding in Delhi on 5 October 2025.","details":null,"id":"4248","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"India Tour Opened in Bengaluru","year":"15 Aug 2025"},{"description":"Raina released his debut stand-up comedy special 'Still Alive' on YouTube, filmed at Good Shepherd Auditorium in Bengaluru, marking his return after a year and directly addressing the India's Got Latent controversy and his journey through it.","details":null,"id":"4249","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Released Still Alive Special","year":"07 Apr 2026"},{"description":"The over-one-hour-long 'Still Alive' special clocked 22 million views within the first 24 hours of release, one of the biggest openings ever for an Indian YouTube upload.","details":null,"id":"4250","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"22 Million Views in 24 Hours","year":"08 Apr 2026"},{"description":"Within two weeks, 'Still Alive' crossed 53.7 million views with over 3.8 million likes, becoming the most-watched full-length stand-up comedy special in the world on YouTube from a single upload.","details":null,"id":"4251","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Became Most-Watched Comedy Special","year":"21 Apr 2026"},{"description":"The special crossed 54.2 million views, cementing its global YouTube record and turning Raina's biggest controversy into a record-breaking comeback widely covered by Indian and international media.","details":null,"id":"4252","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Crossed 54 Million Views Record","year":"23 Apr 2026"},{"description":"Raina was felicitated by Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis at a Maharashtra Cyber awareness event in Mumbai for his contribution to the state's cyber-awareness campaign, which launched the short film 'Digital Arrest' and the 1930 Maharashtra Cyber Anthem.","details":null,"id":"4253","side":"positive","timeline_id":"143","title":"Felicitated by CM Fadnavis","year":"26 Aug 2026"},{"description":"Gyanesh Kumar was born in Agra, Uttar Pradesh, into a middle-class family with strong academic and medical backgrounds.","details":null,"id":"4256","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Born in Agra, Uttar Pradesh","year":"27 JAN 1964"},{"description":"Kumar completed his initial schooling in Agra, where he was recognized as a top-performing student from an early age.","details":null,"id":"4257","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Early schooling in Agra","year":"1970s"},{"description":"He attended Colvin Taluqdars' College in Lucknow for his higher secondary education, topping his class in both Class 10 and Class 12 examinations.","details":null,"id":"4258","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Secondary education at Colvin Taluqdars' College","year":"1980s"},{"description":"Kumar secured admission to the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) Kanpur after clearing the competitive JEE Main and Advanced examinations.","details":null,"id":"4259","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Entered IIT Kanpur","year":"1981"},{"description":"He earned a Bachelor of Technology degree in Civil Engineering from IIT Kanpur, receiving academic excellence recognition for his performance.","details":null,"id":"4260","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Graduated with B.Tech in Civil Engineering","year":"1985"},{"description":"After graduation, Kumar began his professional career at HUDCO (Housing and Urban Development Corporation) in Delhi, working there for approximately one year.","details":null,"id":"4261","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Joined HUDCO, Delhi","year":"1985"},{"description":"Kumar cleared the UPSC Civil Services Examination and joined the IAS as part of the 1988 batch, allotted to the Kerala cadre.","details":null,"id":"4262","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Joined Indian Administrative Service","year":"1988"},{"description":"His first field assignment was as Sub-Collector in Pathanamthitta, Kerala, marking the beginning of his administrative career in the state.","details":null,"id":"4263","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"First posting as Sub-Collector","year":"1990"},{"description":"Kumar held the position of Sub-Collector in Adoor, Kerala, gaining experience in district-level administration and revenue management.","details":null,"id":"4264","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Served as Sub-Collector of Adoor","year":"Early 1990s"},{"description":"He served as Managing Director of the Kerala State Development Corporation for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes, focusing on welfare and development initiatives.","details":null,"id":"4265","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"MD of Kerala State Development Corporation for SC/ST","year":"1990s"},{"description":"Kumar was appointed Municipal Commissioner of the Corporation of Cochin (Kochi), overseeing urban governance and municipal administration.","details":null,"id":"4266","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Municipal Commissioner of Kochi Corporation","year":"1990s"},{"description":"He served as Managing Director of the Kerala State Cooperative Bank, managing financial operations and cooperative banking initiatives in the state.","details":null,"id":"4267","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"MD of Kerala State Cooperative Bank","year":"1990s"},{"description":"Kumar was posted as District Collector of Ernakulam, one of Kerala's key districts, where he earned recognition for public-spirited administration.","details":null,"id":"4268","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"District Collector of Ernakulam","year":"Late 1990s"},{"description":"He held the position of Secretary of the Goshree Islands Development Authority, involved in infrastructure and development projects in the Kochi region.","details":null,"id":"4269","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Secretary of Goshree Islands Development Authority","year":"Late 1990s"},{"description":"Kumar served as Managing Director of the Trivandrum Airport Development Society, contributing to aviation infrastructure development in Kerala.","details":null,"id":"4270","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"MD of Trivandrum Airport Development Society","year":"Late 1990s"},{"description":"He was posted as Resident Commissioner of Kerala House in New Delhi, representing the Kerala government at the national capital.","details":null,"id":"4271","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Resident Commissioner of Kerala House, New Delhi","year":"Early 2000s"},{"description":"Kumar served as Secretary to the Government of Kerala, handling diverse departments including Finance Resources, Public Works, and Food & Civil Supplies.","details":null,"id":"4272","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Secretary in Kerala Government","year":"Early 2000s"},{"description":"He began his second stint at the Centre as Joint Secretary (Defence Production) in the Ministry of Defence during the UPA government.","details":null,"id":"4273","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Joined Ministry of Defence as Joint Secretary","year":"2007"},{"description":"During his tenure at the Defence Ministry, Kumar was tasked with modernising all defence shipyards and Mishra Dhatu Nigam Limited (MIDHANI).","details":null,"id":"4274","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Modernised defence shipyards and MIDHANI","year":"2007–2012"},{"description":"Kumar concluded his five-year assignment at the Ministry of Defence, having contributed to defence production and infrastructure modernisation.","details":null,"id":"4275","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Completed Defence Ministry tenure","year":"2012"},{"description":"After his Defence Ministry posting, he resumed his role as Resident Commissioner of Kerala in New Delhi for an additional four-year period.","details":null,"id":"4276","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Returned to Kerala as Resident Commissioner","year":"2012"},{"description":"Kumar was transferred to the Union Home Ministry in May 2016 as Joint Secretary in the Kashmir Division, then headed by Home Minister Rajnath Singh.","details":null,"id":"4277","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Appointed Joint Secretary in Home Ministry","year":"2016"},{"description":"He oversaw administrative and policy matters related to Jammu and Kashmir during a period of significant political and security developments in the region.","details":null,"id":"4278","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Handled Kashmir Division at Home Ministry","year":"2016–2019"},{"description":"Kumar was elevated to the position of Additional Secretary in the Ministry of Home Affairs, expanding his responsibilities in national security and internal affairs.","details":null,"id":"4279","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Promoted to Additional Secretary in Home Ministry","year":"2018"},{"description":"After Amit Shah became Home Minister, Kumar was involved in drafting the Jammu and Kashmir Reorganisation Bill that abrogated Article 370 and bifurcated the state into two Union Territories.","details":null,"id":"4280","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Key role in Article 370 abrogation","year":"2019"},{"description":"He continued to lead the Jammu and Kashmir Division in the Home Ministry, handling policy implementation and security scenarios following the abrogation.","details":null,"id":"4281","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Headed J&K desk post-abrogation","year":"2019"},{"description":"During his tenure in the Home Ministry, Kumar played a key role in setting up the Shri Ram Janmabhoomi Teertha Kshetra Trust after the Supreme Court's Ayodhya verdict.","details":null,"id":"4282","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Oversaw Ram Janmabhoomi Trust formation","year":"2019–2021"},{"description":"In May 2021, Kumar was appointed Secretary of the Ministry of Parliamentary Affairs in the Government of India.","details":null,"id":"4283","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Appointed Secretary of Parliamentary Affairs","year":"2021"},{"description":"He was appointed Secretary of the newly formed Ministry of Cooperation in May 2022, a department directly overseen by Home Minister Amit Shah.","details":null,"id":"4284","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Became Secretary of Cooperation Ministry","year":"2022"},{"description":"Kumar superannuated from the Indian Administrative Service after completing his tenure as Secretary in the Ministry of Cooperation.","details":null,"id":"4286","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Retired from IAS service","year":"31 JAN 2024"},{"description":"Kumar assumed charge as Election Commissioner shortly before the schedule for the 2024 Lok Sabha elections was announced. He was appointed as one of two new Election Commissioners by the PM-led selection committee, joining the three-member Election Commission of India.","details":null,"id":"4287","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Joined EC before Lok Sabha elections as Election Commissioner","year":"15 MAR 2024"},{"description":"Following the retirement of Rajiv Kumar, Gyanesh Kumar took charge as India's 26th Chief Election Commissioner.","details":null,"id":"4289","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Became 26th Chief Election Commissioner","year":"19 FEB 2025"},{"description":"As CEC, Kumar's tenure is scheduled to last until January 26, 2029, covering multiple Assembly elections and the 2029 Lok Sabha polls.","details":null,"id":"4290","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Tenure extends to January 2029","year":"FEB 2025"},{"description":"IIT Kanpur conferred its highest alumni honour, the Distinguished Alumni Award 2025, on Kumar during its 66th Foundation Day celebration.","details":null,"id":"4291","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Received IIT Kanpur Distinguished Alumni Award","year":"NOV 2025"},{"description":"As CEC, Kumar introduced reforms and modernisation efforts under the banner of 'EC 2.0' to improve electoral processes and voter engagement.","details":null,"id":"4292","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Launched EC 2.0 initiatives","year":"2025–2026"},{"description":"Two Election Commissioners formally objected at least 14 times over 10 months to decisions related to the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls, citing concerns about voter deletions and decision-making processes.","details":null,"id":"4293","side":"negative","timeline_id":"144","title":"Faced internal objections over SIR","year":"NOV 2025–AUG 2026"},{"description":"An Indian Express investigation revealed the internal objections, sparking political controversy and opposition demands for Kumar's removal as CEC.","details":null,"id":"4294","side":"negative","timeline_id":"144","title":"SIR controversy becomes public","year":"23 SEP 2026"},{"description":"Opposition parties mounted fierce attacks on Kumar, accusing him of running the poll panel as a 'one-man autocracy' and calling for his impeachment and arrest.","details":null,"id":"4295","side":"negative","timeline_id":"144","title":"Opposition demands impeachment and arrest","year":"23 SEP 2026"},{"description":"The Election Commission responded that differing views are normal in deliberations and maintained that all decisions, including those on SIR, were taken unanimously.","details":null,"id":"4296","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"EC defends unanimous decision-making","year":"24 SEP 2026"},{"description":"Legal challenges were filed in court seeking a judicial probe, contempt proceedings, and quashing of SIR decisions amid intensifying protests over the controversy.","details":null,"id":"4297","side":"negative","timeline_id":"144","title":"Petitions seek probe and contempt action","year":"25 SEP 2026"},{"description":"Despite political backlash and internal dissent reports, Kumar remains in office as Chief Election Commissioner, overseeing ongoing electoral processes.","details":null,"id":"4298","side":"positive","timeline_id":"144","title":"Continues as CEC amid scrutiny","year":"26 SEP 2026"},{"description":"Bhasker was born in Delhi to former Indian Navy officer C. Uday Bhaskar and cinema studies academic Ira Bhaskar.","details":null,"id":"4299","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Born in Delhi","year":"09 Apr 1988"},{"description":"Before entering films, Bhasker attended Sardar Patel Vidyalaya in New Delhi. Her school graduation year is not publicly verified.","details":null,"id":"4300","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Completes Delhi Schooling","year":"2009"},{"description":"Before moving into films, Bhasker earned a bachelor's degree in English literature from Miranda House, University of Delhi. A verified graduation year is unavailable.","details":null,"id":"4301","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Studies English Literature","year":"2009"},{"description":"Bhasker completed a master's degree in sociology at Jawaharlal Nehru University in New Delhi. She performed in amateur street plays there; a verified degree completion year is unavailable.","details":null,"id":"4302","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Earns Sociology Master's","year":"2009"},{"description":"Before her film career, Bhasker worked with N. K. Sharma's Act One theatre group in Delhi.","details":null,"id":"4303","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Works in Delhi Theatre","year":"2009"},{"description":"After completing her master's examinations, Bhasker moved to Mumbai with a friend to seek acting work. In a later interview, she recalled difficulty finding accommodation for two single women.","details":null,"id":"4304","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Moves to Mumbai","year":"2009"},{"description":"Madholal Keep Walking became Bhasker's first released film, although she had shot another project earlier. The drama did not succeed commercially.","details":null,"id":"4305","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Makes First Film Release","year":"27 Aug 2010"},{"description":"Bhasker played Radhika Talwar in Sanjay Leela Bhansali's drama Guzaarish.","details":null,"id":"4306","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Appears in Guzaarish","year":"19 Nov 2010"},{"description":"She played Payal, the protagonist's friend, in Tanu Weds Manu. The successful film brought her wider recognition.","details":null,"id":"4307","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Breaks Through as Payal","year":"25 Feb 2011"},{"description":"Her performance in Tanu Weds Manu earned a Filmfare nomination for Best Supporting Actress.","details":null,"id":"4308","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Receives First Filmfare Nomination","year":"2012"},{"description":"Bhasker won the Zee Cine Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for Tanu Weds Manu.","details":null,"id":"4309","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Zee Cine Award","year":"2012"},{"description":"Bhasker played the title role in Listen... Amaya, one of her early lead film roles.","details":null,"id":"4310","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Leads Listen Amaya","year":"01 Feb 2013"},{"description":"She appeared in the Hindi crime drama Aurangzeb.","details":null,"id":"4311","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Appears in Aurangzeb","year":"17 May 2013"},{"description":"Bhasker played Bindiya in Aanand L. Rai's Raanjhanaa. The role brought her another Filmfare nomination for Best Supporting Actress.","details":null,"id":"4312","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Plays Bindiya in Raanjhanaa","year":"21 Jun 2013"},{"description":"Bhasker later recalled considering a return to Delhi after a period of unreleased films and limited opportunities, shortly before she was offered Raanjhanaa.","details":null,"id":"4313","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Considers Leaving Mumbai","year":"2013"},{"description":"Bhasker won the Screen Award for Best Supporting Actress for Raanjhanaa.","details":null,"id":"4314","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Screen Supporting Award","year":"14 Jan 2014"},{"description":"She shared the Zee Cine Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for Raanjhanaa with Divya Dutta, who was recognized for Bhaag Milkha Bhaag.","details":null,"id":"4315","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Second Zee Award","year":"2014"},{"description":"Bhasker presented Samvidhaan, Shyam Benegal's television series about the making of India's Constitution. It aired on Rajya Sabha TV.","details":null,"id":"4316","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Presents Constitution Series","year":"2014"},{"description":"She starred in the Hindi horror film Machhli Jal Ki Rani Hai.","details":null,"id":"4317","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Stars in Horror Film","year":"13 Jun 2014"},{"description":"Bhasker reprised her role as Payal in the commercially successful sequel Tanu Weds Manu Returns.","details":null,"id":"4318","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Returns as Payal","year":"22 May 2015"},{"description":"She received the Best Actress award at China's Silk Road International Film Festival for Nil Battey Sannata, ahead of the film's Indian theatrical release.","details":null,"id":"4319","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins International Acting Prize","year":"Sep 2015"},{"description":"Bhasker began hosting the film-song programme Rangoli on DD National.","details":null,"id":"4320","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Begins Hosting Rangoli","year":"Nov 2015"},{"description":"She played Rajkumari Chandrika in Prem Ratan Dhan Payo, a major commercial release starring Salman Khan and Sonam Kapoor.","details":null,"id":"4321","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Appears in Prem Ratan","year":"12 Nov 2015"},{"description":"Bhasker appeared in X: Past Is Present, an anthology film made by multiple directors.","details":null,"id":"4322","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Joins Ensemble Film","year":"20 Nov 2015"},{"description":"Bhasker played Chanda, a domestic worker raising a teenage daughter, in Nil Battey Sannata. The lead role became a major milestone in her film career.","details":null,"id":"4323","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Leads Nil Battey Sannata","year":"22 Apr 2016"},{"description":"She won a Best Actress award at the Jagran Film Festival for Nil Battey Sannata.","details":null,"id":"4324","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Jagran Acting Award","year":"2016"},{"description":"It's Not That Simple premiered on Voot with Bhasker in the lead role of Meera.","details":null,"id":"4325","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Enters Streaming Drama","year":"21 Oct 2016"},{"description":"Bhasker received the Screen critics' prize for Best Actress for Nil Battey Sannata. The ceremony took place in December 2016 and is also listed in some awards records under 2017.","details":null,"id":"4326","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Screen Critics Award","year":"Dec 2016"},{"description":"She played the title role of a performer confronting sexual harassment in Anaarkali of Aarah. The performance later earned a Filmfare critics' nomination.","details":null,"id":"4327","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Leads Anaarkali of Aarah","year":"24 Mar 2017"},{"description":"Bhasker won the Jagran Film Festival's Best Actress award for Anaarkali of Aarah.","details":null,"id":"4328","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wins Jagran Actress Award","year":"2017"},{"description":"Bhasker published an open letter criticizing the depiction of jauhar in Padmaavat. The letter drew substantial public criticism and online abuse.","details":null,"id":"4329","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Challenges Padmaavat Ending","year":"Jan 2018"},{"description":"She played Sakshi in the ensemble comedy Veere Di Wedding. The performance subsequently earned her a Filmfare nomination for Best Supporting Actress.","details":null,"id":"4330","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Stars in Veere Di Wedding","year":"01 Jun 2018"},{"description":"Bhasker reprised her role as Meera in the second season of It's Not That Simple.","details":null,"id":"4331","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Returns to Streaming Series","year":"14 Dec 2018"},{"description":"She received another Filmfare Best Supporting Actress nomination for Veere Di Wedding.","details":null,"id":"4332","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Receives Third Supporting Nomination","year":"2019"},{"description":"Bhasker publicly opposed the Citizenship Amendment Act and participated in protests against it.","details":null,"id":"4333","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Opposes Citizenship Law","year":"Dec 2019"},{"description":"The streaming series Rasbhari premiered with Bhasker playing multiple roles.","details":null,"id":"4334","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Stars in Rasbhari","year":"25 Jun 2020"},{"description":"Bhasker played police officer Radha Nautiyal in the Eros Now crime series Flesh.","details":null,"id":"4335","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Leads Crime Series Flesh","year":"Aug 2020"},{"description":"She played an aspiring stand-up comedian in the Netflix series Bhaag Beanie Bhaag, her third streaming-series release of 2020.","details":null,"id":"4336","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Leads Bhaag Beanie Bhaag","year":"Dec 2020"},{"description":"The MX Player series Aapkey Kamrey Mein Koi Rehta Hai began streaming with Bhasker playing Mausam.","details":null,"id":"4337","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Joins Horror Comedy","year":"22 Jan 2021"},{"description":"Bhasker starred as Shivangi in Jahaan Chaar Yaar, her first listed theatrical feature release since Veere Di Wedding.","details":null,"id":"4338","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Returns to Theatres","year":"16 Sep 2022"},{"description":"She walked with Rahul Gandhi during the Bharat Jodo Yatra in Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh.","details":null,"id":"4339","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Joins Bharat Jodo Yatra","year":"01 Dec 2022"},{"description":"Bhasker and political activist Fahad Ahmad registered their marriage under India's Special Marriage Act.","details":null,"id":"4340","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Registers Marriage to Ahmad","year":"06 Jan 2023"},{"description":"Bhasker publicly announced her marriage to Ahmad. The couple later held traditional wedding celebrations in March.","details":null,"id":"4341","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Announces Marriage Publicly","year":"16 Feb 2023"},{"description":"Bhasker completed filming Mrs Falani, a project in which she plays multiple characters. Its completion did not amount to a theatrical release.","details":null,"id":"4342","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Wraps Mrs Falani","year":"May 2023"},{"description":"Bhasker gave birth to her daughter, Raabiyaa, with Fahad Ahmad.","details":null,"id":"4343","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Welcomes Daughter Raabiyaa","year":"23 Sep 2023"},{"description":"Ahmad lost the Anushakti Nagar seat in the Maharashtra Assembly election to Sana Malik by 3,378 votes. Bhasker, who supported his campaign, questioned aspects of the vote count.","details":null,"id":"4344","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Husband Loses Assembly Election","year":"23 Nov 2024"},{"description":"Bhasker said in an interview that she believed her political views had led to her being blacklisted for acting work. This was her account of the career setback, not an independently established industry-wide ban.","details":null,"id":"4345","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Describes Career Setback","year":"23 Jan 2025"},{"description":"Bhasker and Ahmad appeared together on Pati Patni Aur Panga, which premiered on Colors TV.","details":null,"id":"4346","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Joins Couples Reality Show","year":"02 Aug 2025"},{"description":"Bhasker and Ahmad finished as third runners-up, or fourth place, on Pati Patni Aur Panga.","details":null,"id":"4347","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Finishes Fourth on Show","year":"Nov 2025"},{"description":"After renewed criticism of her comments about Padmaavat's jauhar sequence, Bhasker said her remarks had been mistranslated and denied calling Queen Padmavati or women who performed sati cowards.","details":null,"id":"4348","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Clarifies Jauhar Remarks","year":"02 Sep 2026"},{"description":"Bhasker joined the cast of the second season of the reality show Rise & Fall, which premiered on this date.","details":null,"id":"4349","side":"positive","timeline_id":"145","title":"Enters Rise and Fall","year":"26 Sep 2026"},{"description":"During Rise & Fall, Bhasker disclosed that two IVF attempts before her marriage had been unsuccessful. She did not give dates for the treatments.","details":null,"id":"4350","side":"negative","timeline_id":"145","title":"Shares Earlier IVF Setbacks","year":"29 Sep 2026"},{"description":"Shehzad Poonawalla was born on October 17, 1987, in Pune, Maharashtra, India, into an Aga Khani Shia Muslim family.","details":null,"id":"4351","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Born in Pune, Maharashtra","year":"17 Oct 1987"},{"description":"Shehzad's father, Sarfraz Poonawalla, a businessman, died when Shehzad was just 5 years old, leaving his mother Yasmin Poonawalla to raise him and his older brother Tehseen.","details":null,"id":"4352","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Father Sarfraz Poonawalla passes away","year":"1992"},{"description":"Shehzad completed his early schooling at St. Vincent's High School in Pune, Maharashtra.","details":null,"id":"4353","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Attends St. Vincent's High School","year":"YYYY"},{"description":"He pursued and completed a Bachelor of Commerce (B.Com) degree from Ness Wadia College of Commerce in Pune.","details":null,"id":"4354","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Graduates from Ness Wadia College","year":"YYYY"},{"description":"Shehzad earned his Bachelor of Laws (LLB) degree from Savitribai Phule Pune University (formerly University of Pune) in 2008, qualifying as a lawyer.","details":null,"id":"4355","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Completes LLB from Pune University","year":"2008"},{"description":"After completing his law course, Shehzad interned with Congress leader Suresh Kalmadi before joining the All India Congress Committee (AICC) as a volunteer.","details":null,"id":"4356","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Interns with Suresh Kalmadi","year":"2008"},{"description":"Shehzad began his political career by joining the Indian National Congress in 2008, starting as a volunteer.","details":null,"id":"4357","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Joins Indian National Congress","year":"2008"},{"description":"He interned with the Congress party's media research team in Delhi after completing his course in 2008.","details":null,"id":"4358","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Joins AICC media research team","year":"2008"},{"description":"From June 2009 to December 2010, Shehzad worked in the office of Manish Tewari, then a minister in UPA-2.","details":null,"id":"4359","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Works with Manish Tewari's office","year":"2009"},{"description":"Shehzad rose to become the Vice-President of the Pune wing of the National Students' Union of India (NSUI), the student wing of the Congress party.","details":null,"id":"4360","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Becomes NSUI Pune Vice-President","year":"2010"},{"description":"He served as an Additional Private Secretary (APS) to Rajeev Shukla when Shukla became a minister of state in UPA-2 in 2011.","details":null,"id":"4361","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Becomes APS to Rajeev Shukla","year":"2011"},{"description":"Shehzad was involved as a petitioner in the 2013 National Commission for Minorities housing discrimination case, advocating against communal discrimination in housing.","details":null,"id":"4362","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Petitioner in NCM housing case","year":"2013"},{"description":"After eight years of voluntary work, Shehzad was elevated to the position of Secretary in the Maharashtra Pradesh Congress Committee in 2016.","details":null,"id":"4363","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Appointed Maharashtra Congress Secretary","year":"2016"},{"description":"Shehzad publicly challenged the Congress presidential election process, alleging it was rigged to favor Rahul Gandhi's elevation as party president, and demanded a merit-based election.","details":null,"id":"4364","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Challenges Congress presidential election","year":"Nov 2017"},{"description":"He sent a strongly-worded letter to Rahul Gandhi questioning his elevation and calling the organizational elections a sham, creating a political storm within the Congress.","details":null,"id":"4365","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Writes open letter to Rahul Gandhi","year":"Nov 2017"},{"description":"Following his public rebellion, Shehzad faced isolation within the Congress party, with leaders casting him aside and saying he was never a part of the organization.","details":null,"id":"4366","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Isolated within Congress party","year":"2017"},{"description":"Shehzad alleged that he received threatening calls from unknown numbers warning him to stop his campaign against Rahul Gandhi, along with abusive messages and emails from Congress supporters.","details":null,"id":"4367","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Receives threatening calls","year":"2017"},{"description":"The public fallout over the presidential election controversy led to Shehzad's eventual exit from the Congress party in late 2017.","details":null,"id":"4368","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Exits Indian National Congress","year":"2017"},{"description":"Shehzad formally joined the BJP at the party headquarters in New Delhi in July 2018, in the presence of then Minister of Railways and Coal, Piyush Goyal.","details":null,"id":"4369","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Joins Bharatiya Janata Party","year":"Jul 2018"},{"description":"He accused the Indian National Congress of being involved in a scam related to the National Herald case, alleging that Sonia Gandhi and Rahul Gandhi misappropriated funds, and challenged Rahul Gandhi to a lie detector test.","details":null,"id":"4370","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Accuses INC of National Herald scam","year":"2018"},{"description":"Shehzad filed a petition in the Supreme Court seeking a direction to the Election Commission to debar Rahul Gandhi from contesting the Lok Sabha elections, alleging dual citizenship of India and the United Kingdom.","details":null,"id":"4371","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Files petition against Rahul Gandhi","year":"2019"},{"description":"The Supreme Court dismissed Shehzad's petition to debar Rahul Gandhi from contesting elections, with the bench questioning the timing and basis of the allegations.","details":null,"id":"4372","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Supreme Court dismisses petition","year":"May 2019"},{"description":"Shehzad was booked by the Delhi Police for allegedly spreading fake news and communal hatred on social media in connection with the February 2020 Delhi riots, accused of posting inflammatory and misleading tweets.","details":null,"id":"4373","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Booked by Delhi Police","year":"Feb 2020"},{"description":"By 2021, Shehzad had been appointed as a BJP National Spokesperson, becoming one of the party's most recognizable faces on prime-time TV debates.","details":null,"id":"4374","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Appointed BJP National Spokesperson","year":"2021"},{"description":"In December 2021, he was additionally placed in charge of the Delhi unit's IT and social media department, expanding his responsibilities within the party.","details":null,"id":"4375","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Given charge of Delhi BJP IT cell","year":"Dec 2021"},{"description":"Shehzad was arrested by the Mumbai Police for allegedly cheating a woman of Rs 3 crore on the pretext of investing in a film project, and was also accused of threatening and blackmailing the woman.","details":null,"id":"4376","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Arrested in Mumbai cheating case","year":"2021"},{"description":"After spending two months in jail, Shehzad was granted bail by a court in the Mumbai cheating case.","details":null,"id":"4377","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Granted bail after two months","year":"2021"},{"description":"In April 2024, Shehzad engaged in a heated TV debate with Congress spokesperson Supriya Shrinate, correcting her on the Director General of Military Operations in Northern Command.","details":null,"id":"4378","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Debates Supriya Shrinate on TV","year":"2024"},{"description":"Shehzad later revealed that he had been considering a transition to the private sector after the 2024 Lok Sabha elections, citing financial and personal circumstances.","details":null,"id":"4379","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Decides to leave politics post-elections","year":"2024"},{"description":"In February 2026, Shehzad alleged that his mother was deliberately run over by a car in a hit-and-run incident in Pune, leaving her seriously injured with a fractured leg and requiring surgery.","details":null,"id":"4380","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Mother injured in hit-and-run","year":"Feb 2026"},{"description":"Shehzad and his brother Tehseen shared CCTV footage of the incident on social media, alleging the driver deliberately struck his mother and fled the scene, and appealed for police action.","details":null,"id":"4381","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Shares CCTV footage publicly","year":"Feb 2026"},{"description":"In July 2026, Shehzad updated his X (formerly Twitter) bio, removing all references to the BJP and his role as national spokesperson, sparking speculation about his future.","details":null,"id":"4382","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Updates X bio, drops BJP tag","year":"Jul 2026"},{"description":"Shehzad submitted an unconditional resignation from the BJP on July 30, 2026, citing pressing financial and personal circumstances.","details":null,"id":"4383","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Submits resignation to BJP","year":"30 Jul 2026"},{"description":"In his resignation letter to BJP chief Nitin Nabin, Shehzad stated that he would continue to support the vision and work of PM Modi and the BJP wherever possible.","details":null,"id":"4386","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"States will support Modi vision","year":"Aug 2026"},{"description":"Days after resigning from the BJP, Shehzad announced his debut on reality television, joining Season 2 of the Prime Video show Rise & Fall, premiering September 26, 2026.","details":null,"id":"4389","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Joins Rise & Fall Season 2","year":"26 Sep 2026"},{"description":"During Episode 3 of Rise & Fall 2, a heated discussion over politics and religion escalated into a physical scuffle with contestant Siwet Tomar, leaving Shehzad's shirt torn.","details":null,"id":"4390","side":"negative","timeline_id":"146","title":"Physical altercation on show","year":"29 Sep 2026"},{"description":"As of 2026, Shehzad Poonawalla remains unmarried and does not have any children, focusing on his career and family responsibilities.","details":null,"id":"4392","side":"positive","timeline_id":"146","title":"Unmarried, no children","year":"2026"}]}$tlw_snapshot$::jsonb);
CREATE TEMP TABLE tlw_expected_timelines ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT timeline->>'id' AS timeline_id
FROM tlw_snapshot, jsonb_array_elements(document->'timelines') AS source(timeline);
ALTER TABLE tlw_expected_timelines ADD PRIMARY KEY (timeline_id);

CREATE TEMP TABLE tlw_approved_positions ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT timeline->>'id' AS timeline_id, event_id, ordinal * 10::bigint AS position
FROM tlw_snapshot,
     jsonb_array_elements(document->'timelines') AS source(timeline),
     jsonb_array_elements_text(timeline->'event_ids') WITH ORDINALITY AS sequence(event_id, ordinal);
ALTER TABLE tlw_approved_positions ADD PRIMARY KEY (event_id);
ALTER TABLE tlw_approved_positions ADD UNIQUE (timeline_id, position);

CREATE TEMP TABLE tlw_expected_events ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT event->>'id' AS event_id, event->>'timeline_id' AS timeline_id, event AS content
FROM tlw_snapshot, jsonb_array_elements(document->'events') AS source(event);
ALTER TABLE tlw_expected_events ADD PRIMARY KEY (event_id);
CREATE TEMP TABLE tlw_previous_updated_at ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT id, updated_at FROM public.timelines;

DO $validation$
BEGIN
  IF (SELECT count(*) FROM public.timelines) <> 97
     OR (SELECT count(*) FROM public.events) <> 3534
     OR (SELECT count(*) FROM tlw_expected_timelines) <> 97
     OR (SELECT count(*) FROM tlw_approved_positions) <> 3534
     OR (SELECT count(*) FROM tlw_expected_events) <> 3534 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Approved snapshot counts do not match; aborting backfill';
  END IF;
  IF EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.timelines AS live FULL JOIN tlw_expected_timelines AS expected
      ON live.id::text = expected.timeline_id
    WHERE live.id IS NULL OR expected.timeline_id IS NULL
  ) OR EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.events AS live FULL JOIN tlw_approved_positions AS expected
      ON live.id::text = expected.event_id AND live.timeline_id::text = expected.timeline_id
    WHERE live.id IS NULL OR expected.event_id IS NULL
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Approved timeline/event membership changed; aborting backfill';
  END IF;
  IF EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.events AS live FULL JOIN tlw_expected_events AS expected
      ON live.id::text = expected.event_id AND live.timeline_id::text = expected.timeline_id
    WHERE live.id IS NULL OR expected.event_id IS NULL OR
      jsonb_build_object('id', live.id::text, 'timeline_id', live.timeline_id::text,
        'year', live.year, 'title', live.title, 'description', live.description,
        'side', live.side, 'details', live.details) IS DISTINCT FROM expected.content
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Approved event content changed; aborting backfill';
  END IF;
END;
$validation$;

-- Feature #1's existing trigger ignores position-only updates. Do not disable it.
UPDATE public.events AS event SET sort_order = approved.position
FROM tlw_approved_positions AS approved
WHERE event.id::text = approved.event_id AND event.timeline_id::text = approved.timeline_id;

DO $verification$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.events WHERE sort_order IS NULL)
     OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.events GROUP BY timeline_id, sort_order HAVING count(*) > 1)
     OR EXISTS (
       SELECT 1 FROM public.events AS event JOIN tlw_approved_positions AS approved
         ON event.id::text = approved.event_id AND event.timeline_id::text = approved.timeline_id
       WHERE event.sort_order IS DISTINCT FROM approved.position
     ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Backfill position verification failed';
  END IF;
  IF EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM public.timelines AS live JOIN tlw_previous_updated_at AS previous USING (id)
    WHERE live.updated_at IS DISTINCT FROM previous.updated_at
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Backfill changed timeline updated_at; rolling back';
  END IF;
END;
$verification$;

ALTER TABLE public.events ALTER COLUMN sort_order SET NOT NULL;
-- Signed values permit Top insertion without renumbering existing events.
-- This constraint also supplies the composite ordering index.
ALTER TABLE public.events ADD CONSTRAINT events_timeline_sort_order_unique
  UNIQUE (timeline_id, sort_order) DEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE;
COMMIT;
